nalysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"uuid\":\"1e058052-460b-49c9-b421-09db47304ebf\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:20:48.607Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"d277e756-5b20-4b09-8cfe-1366c2d8bd33\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"1e058052-460b-49c9-b421-09db47304ebf\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d139098daa76558cf7f14d9d4ac2d\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Now let me:1. Move `isFpMulMadd` to BEFORE `isFpDataProc1Source` in the decoder routing (it's currently checked at line 3812, but needs to be before line 3808)\\n2. Tighten `isFpDataProc1Source` by changing 'X','X','X','X' at op2 to '1','X','X','X' (requiring bit22=1)First, let me update the pattern definition and then the routing.Actually, the order in the source file is:\\n1. Pattern definitions (any order - no impact)\\n2. Router checks (order matters!)Router checks:\\n\\n\\n- isFpMulMadd is at line 3812 (CHECKED LAST)- isFpDataProc1Source is at line 3808 (CHECKED BEFORE isFpMulMadd!)So `isFpDataProc1Source` is checked BEFORE `isFpMulMadd`. I need to move the `isFpMulMadd` check BEFORE `isFpDataProc1Source` in the router.But I also need to make the patterns mutually exclusive. If I just move the check, then both patterns would match. I need to tighten `isFpDataProc1Source` to NOT match FMLA/FMLS. Let me do both:1. Tighten `isFpDataProc1Source` by requiring bit22=1\\n\\n2. Move `isFpMulMadd` check before `isFpDataProc1Source` in the router\",\"signature\":\"ac2740e708954358c15650f0f62288618dedbeadd