807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d1d17bf96d92692a4dfed2b658079\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_function_gnzacgktxbvm_1\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5/configs/example/arm/devices.py\",\"offset\":98,\"limit\":120}}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":529,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":52647,\"output_tokens\":106,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"968224cf-1ba0-4b17-a0ec-b88af0163d5e\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:01:30.972Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"968224cf-1ba0-4b17-a0ec-b88af0163d5e\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"520da623-e17e-4efe-b292-47222de157e3\",\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_function_gnzacgktxbvm_1\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"98\\tclass ArmCpuCluster(CpuCluster):\\n99\\t    def __init__(\\n100\\t        self,\\n101\\t        system,\\n102\\t        num_cpus,\\n103\\t        cpu_clock,\\n104\\t        cpu_voltage,\\n105\\t        cpu_type,\\n106\\t        l1i_type,\\n107\\t        l1d_type,\\n108\\t        l2_type,\\n109\\t        tarmac_gen=False,\\n110\\t        tarmac_dest=None,\\n111\\t    ):\\n112\\t        super().__init__()\\n113\\t        self._cpu_type = cpu_type\\n114\\t        self._l1i_type = l1i_type\\n115\\t        self._l1d_type = l1d_type\\n116\\t        self._l2_type = l2_type\\n117\\t\\n118\\t        assert num_cpus > 0\\n119\\t\\n120\\t        self.voltage_domain = VoltageDomain(voltage=cpu_voltage)\\n121\\t        self.clk_domain = SrcClockDomain(\\n122\\t            clock=cpu_clock, voltage_domain=self.voltage_domain\\n123\\t        )\\n124\\t\\n125\\t        self.generate_cpus(cpu_type, num_cpus)\\n126\\t\\n127\\t        for cpu in self.cpus:\\n128\\t            if tarmac_gen:\\n129\\t                cpu.tracer = TarmacTracer()\\n130\\t                if tarmac_dest is not None:\\n131\\t                    cpu.tracer.outfile = tarmac_dest\\n132\\t\\n133\\t        system.addCpuCluster(self)\\n134\\t\\n135\\t    def addL1(self):\\n136\\t        for cpu in self.cpus:\\n137\\t            l1i = None if self._l1i_type is None else self._l1i_type()\\n138\\t            l1d = None if self._l1d_type is None else self._l1d_type()\\n139\\t            cpu.addPrivateSplitL1Caches(l1i, l1d)\\n140\\t\\n141\\t    def addL2(self, clk_domain):\\n142\\t        if self._l2_type is None:\\n143\\t            return\\n144\\t        self.toL2Bus = L2XBar(width=64, clk_domain=clk_domain)\\n145\\t        self.l2 = self._l2_type()\\n146\\t        for cpu in self.cpus:\\n147\\t            cpu.connectCachedPorts(self.toL2Bus.cpu_side_ports)\\n148\\t        self.toL2Bus.mem_side_ports = self.l2.cpu_side\\n149\\t\\n150\\t    def addPMUs(\\n151\\t        self,\\n152\\t        ints,\\n153\\t        events=[],\\n154\\t        stat_counters=[],\\n155\\t        exit_sim_on_control=False,\\n156\\t        exit_sim_on_interrupt=False,\\n157\\t    ):\\n158\\t        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n159\\t        Instantiates 1 ArmPMU per PE. The method is accepting a list of\\n160\\t        interrupt numbers (ints) used by the PMU and a list of events to\\n161\\t        register in it.\\n162\\t\\n163\\t        :param ints: List of interrupt numbers. The code will iterate over\\n164\\t            the cpu list in order and will assign to every cpu in the cluster\\n165\\t            a PMU with the matching interrupt.\\n166\\t        :type ints: List[int]\\n167\\t        :param events: Additional events to be measured by the PMUs\\n168\\t        :type events: List[Union[ProbeEvent, SoftwareIncrement]]\\n169\\t        :param exit_sim_on_control: If true, exit the sim loop when the PMU is\\n170\\t            enabled, disabled, or reset.\\n171\\t        :type exit_on_control: bool\\n172\\t        :param exit_sim_on_interrupt: If true, exit the sim loop when the PMU\\n173\\t            triggers an interrupt.\\n174\\t        :type exit_on_control: bool\\n175\\t\\n176\\t        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n177\\t        # If ALL option has been passed, simply enable everything\\n178\\t        stat_counters = (\\n179\\t            EventTypeId.vals if \\\"ALL\\\" in stat_counters else stat_counters\\n180\\t        )\\n181\\t\\n182\\t        assert len(ints) == len(self.cpus)\\n183\\t        for cpu, pint in zip(self.cpus, ints):\\n184\\t            int_cls = ArmPPI if pint < 32 else ArmSPI\\n185\\t            for isa in cpu.isa:\\n186\\t                isa.pmu = ArmPMU(interrupt=int_cls(num=pint))\\n187\\t                isa.pmu.exitOnPMUControl = exit_sim_on_control\\n188\\t                isa.pmu.exitOnPMUInterrupt = exit_sim_on_interrupt\\n189\\t                isa.pmu.addArchEvents(\\n190\\t                    cpu=cpu,\\n191\\t                    itb=cpu.mmu.itb,\\n192\\t                    dtb=cpu.mmu.dtb,\\n193\\t                    l2_shared=cpu.mmu.l2_shared,\\n194\\t                    icache=getattr(cpu, \\\"icache\\\", None),\\n195\\t                    dcache=getattr(cpu, \\\"dcache\\\", None),\\n196\\t                    l2cache=getattr(self, \\\"l2\\\", None),\\n197\\t                )\\n198\\t                for ev in events:\\n199\\t                    isa.pmu.addEvent(ev)\\n200\\t\\n201\\t                isa.pmu.statCounters = isa.pmu.archStatCounters(*stat_counters)\\n202\\t\\n203\\t    def connectMemSide(self, bus):\\n204\\t        try:\\n205\\t            self.l2.mem_side = bus.cpu_side_ports\\n206\\t        except AttributeError:\\n207\\t            for cpu in self.cpus:\\n208\\t                cpu.connectCachedPorts(bus.cpu_side_ports)\\n209\\t\\n210\\t\\n211\\tclass AtomicCluster(ArmCpuCluster):\\n212\\t    def __init__(\\n213\\t        self,\\n214\\t        system,\\n215\\t        num_cpus,\\n216\\t        cpu_clock,\\n217\\t        cpu_voltage=\\\"1.0V\\\",\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"uuid\":\"ca3bb42e-4a90-4774-8fac-1dc539627c7e\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:01:31.111Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"968224cf-1ba0-4b17-a0ec-b88af0163d5e\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"ca3bb42e-4a90-4774-8fac-1dc539627c7e\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d1d1b62dc0919fcd40dc1fee6f2bf\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"I don't see any explicit FP/SIMD enabling in the cluster config. The issue is that `AtomicSimpleCPU` doesn't set up FP/SIMD extension registers properly by default. Let me check the AtomicSimpleCPU's ISA configuration and how `checkFPAdvSIMDEnabled64` works.\\n\\nActually, let me look at the backtrace more carefully:\\n```\\n5   gem5.opt                            0x00000001002e2b7c REDACTED + 0\\n6   gem5.opt                            0x00000001007395d8 REDACTED + 248\\n\\n\\n``