ng the pattern from working as expected. I'll instrument the binary directly to see what's actually happening. I need to understand how the ISA parser generates the mask and match values as compile-time constants. For the `isFpMulMadd` pattern, the template recursively builds the mask by setting bits wherever a character isn't 'X', so I need to trace through which bits get constrained for that specific instruction.\\n\\nComputing the mask...\\n\\nSo the mask becomes 0xf9c00000 and the match value is 0x18000000. The generated code creates a lambda that checks if the instruction matches this pattern, which should work correctly. But if the runtime check is still failing despite the compile-time calculation being correct, maybe the generated code isn't actually being compiled into the binary being tested. Let me verify the timestamps and consider whether I should do a clean rebuild to rule out stale object files. I'm checking the build timestamp of the executable against the decoder-ns.o file to see if they align, though I'm realizing I might be looking at this wrong since the object files are stored elsewhere in the build directory.\",\"signature\":\"cfdaddea4ddd90f7bcce87a82bba4762aa4216faf0a34fd6f7742582c39162f8\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":112566},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"eefa6f92-d372-4728-9e37-71bd77f23e31\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:33:31.243Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"eefa6f92-d372-4728-9e37-71bd77f23e31\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d24871ba33d19d9c1b3a77aa83215\",\"type\":\"messa