routes to its decode function since it doesn't check bit23.\\n\\nBut I need to reconsider the actual requirement here—`isFpMulMadd` should match FMLS and FMLA instructions, and the constraint is that `isFpDataProc2Source` must not match these same instructions. The current `isFpDataProc2Source` pattern doesn't have a guard on bit23, so I need to figure out what's preventing FMLS and FMLA from matching it currently. Looking at the mask calculation, when I OR together all those bit extractions, I get 0xF9C00000, which confirms the mask is correct. Now I'm trying to trace through the actual value being checked against this mask.\\n\\nWait, I think I found the issue—the instruction encoding might be in the upper 32 bits of ExtMachInst rather than the lower bits. Let me check how the decoder actually reads and stores the instruction.\",\"signature\":\"77ca246b89bedbc8436905fe4fa36a90d80872efd1250c4f4cc1c1999ed5c603\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":828,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":124410},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"340de482-2af6-4d1f-9152-ff12f12aa76b\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:38:16.802Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"340de482-2af6-4d1f-9152-ff12f12aa76b\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d25988de71a5ac89461ee7471ed68\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me check how `ExtMachInst` is actually constructed - the 32-bit instruction might be in upper bits:\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0