tructure more carefully, the `instBits` field is a 32-bit integer positioned at bits 31:0 of the BitUnion, but there are other bitfield definitions like `Bitfield<63, 62>` that seem to be overlapping with the same bit range. I need to understand how these overlapping fields interact and whether the AArch64 instruction encoding is actually in the upper bits rather than the lower bits. I'm realizing I need to look more carefully at the actual `ExtMachInst` bit layout to understand where the instruction bits are actually stored—the pattern suggests they're in the upper bits rather than the lower 32 bits, but I should verify this directly from the types definition instead of guessing.\",\"signature\":\"987231e8f239fa986aded95fd863b67c572d340da95706a33c7c6c690fc539b4\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":126132},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"d02ab513-663c-4f83-826d-02baaa6cb784\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:38:37.729Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"d02ab513-663c-4f83-826d-02baaa6cb784\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d25bb63dd179d6eeebdf28d07e464\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"`emi.instBits = data` stores the 32-bit instruction at bits 31:0. Let me look at the bitfield definitions that overlap with `instBits`:\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":126132},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",