UID\":\"26450334-b82c-4858-98a2-3f23820daabe\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"4d9676b4-970d-4c37-86d1-4148d1df1dae\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d2c062f4458ae1016f6b98654ab24\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"All debug strings are in the binary, but NONE print. The \\\"DEBUG: READING DATA ONE BYTE AT A TIME!\\\" string is interesting - maybe there's special debugging code in the decoder that reads data byte by byte?\\n\\nBut more importantly - my debug strings ARE in the binary, and none print. This means `decodeInst`, `decodeFpAdvSIMD`, `decodeFpDataProc2Source`, and `Unknown64::execute` are ALL never called!\\n\\nThis is very strange. The backtrace shows:\\n1. `AtomicSimpleCPU::tick()` \\n2. `advancePC()` ← this calls the instruction\\n\\n\\n3. `UndefinedInstruction::invoke()`\\n4. `onUDelay()` ← why is this in the backtrace?\\n\\nThe `UndefinedInstruction::invoke()` is being called, but none of my decode debug prints happen. If the instruction were being decoded properly, I'd see \\\"DEBUG decodeInst ENTRY\\\" first. If it returned Unknown64, I'd see \\\"DEBUG Unknown64::execute\\\". If it triggered the fault at execution, I'd see \\\"DEBUG Unknown64::execute\\\" before \\\"panic\\\". But the panic happens without any debug output, which means the instruction is never being decoded at all.\\n\\nWait, I'm seeing \\\"DEBUG decodeInst ENTRY: machInst=0x1e2e1000\\\" in an earlier run, but not in the current one. The current binary has all the debug strings but they're not being printed, which suggests the compiled code isn't actually calling the decode functions.\\n\\nLooking at the backtrace, the fault is being triggered from `UndefinedInstruction::invoke()` when it's trying to execute the instruction at tick 0. The `UndefinedInstruction` fault must be getting created somewhere in the decode path, but my debug statements inside `Unknown64::execute` aren't firing, which means the fault is being instantiated elsewhere.\\n\\nI'm tracing through the possible decode paths to see where `Unknown64` or `Unknown` objects are being created with that particular fault flag set. The issue is that `Unknown64::execute` contains a `return` statement that produces a fault, but it's never actually being called. I need to figure out which object files contain the main `decodeInst` function that I edited and verify whether those changes actually made it into the final binary.\",\"signature\":\"91b8f4eb72506719492578d59db2e9f2d3d6e37f0834da482a28f28f4a20fded\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":218,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":7,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":133384},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"04e897ac-490e-4b50-872c-7a2c2f5e70ec\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:05:27.905Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"04e897ac-490e-4b50-872c-7a2c2f5e70ec\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d2c062f4458ae1016f6b98654ab24\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The binary has all debug strings but none printed. Let me check if the edited `decode-method.cc.inc` is actually compiled:\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":218,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":7,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":133384}