-bit decode path wouldn't even be involved. I need to figure out what `StaticInst::encoding()` actually returns for an `ArmStaticInst`.\\n\\nLooking at the ARM-specific implementation, `encoding()` is returning the instruction encoding, which comes from the `machInst` field. So if that field contains 0x1e2e1000, then the decode must have happened at some point. But here's the thing - maybe the decode didn't go through `ArmISA::Decoder::decodeInst` at all. The decoder cache in gem5 might be using a completely different decoding path, so the static instruction could be created through a different mechanism entirely.\",\"signature\":\"cb06510269988487d2cb560ae1ba6afab5b0d77ccb0c68d08cbb4de78521e1f8\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":218,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":300,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":146569},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"2015830b-05e8-4c4a-b81d-61b023aa7371\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:15:53.213Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"2015830b-05e8-4c4a-b81d-61b023aa7371\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d2e7b237578cb6104c0a09b26db68\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me check how the decoder cache works - maybe there's a separate decode path:\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":218,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":300,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":146569},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"51804728-aefc-4e1a-948d-8a214c9af0e3\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:15:53.948Z\",\"userType\":\"e