ctly extracts bits 31:28, 27, and 23, confirming the mask is working as intended.\\n\\nNow I'm wondering if I need to update the pattern in the aarch64.isa file, since my previous edit already changed it to include more 'X' characters for the specific bit ranges, but I should verify what the actual current pattern looks like. Looking at the pattern I created, I'm mapping each bit position from 31 down to 10 across the different groups, but I'm noticing a discrepancy with bit 24 — my pattern shows '1' when the actual instruction has '0' there, so I need to fix that mapping.\",\"signature\":\"51ed6c128d7fa7b2680668a7c7f486a6b0d273fb80a9c443f88b5ee6a5981a44\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1183,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":83393},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"22309380-4642-49b4-9deb-ce5db04d18d0\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:13:46.478Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"22309380-4642-49b4-9deb-ce5db04d18d0\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d1fe170184da2e3df5c5aaf24ff83\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I had the wrong bit for position 24. Let me check what the current file has and fix it:\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1183,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":83393},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"153eaf6c-dda1-46e5-8198-e7fb57508ca7\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:13:47.094Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"