nd I also need to double-check the comment on the op1 field. I'm verifying the constraint ordering in the pattern—bit24 is '0' and bit23 is '1'—and making sure the comment matches the corrected values so it accurately reflects what the pattern expects. Verifying the bit constraints for the corrected pattern against the FMLS instruction 0x1e2e1000, confirming that all specified bits match correctly: bits31:28, 27, 24, 23, and 22 all align as expected.\\n\\nThe corrected pattern should now be applied, though I need to verify the exact character count—counting through the bit assignments from bit31 down to bit10 to ensure the pattern has the right number of elements. I'm mapping out how each character in the string corresponds to bit positions, working through the pattern to identify which bits are fixed versus wildcards, then calculating the mask and match values accordingly. For bit24, the correct value is '0', so I'm updating that position in the array.\",\"signature\":\"f0453a7b15afa8639235be804436ed7a61c06e512a913ffad18c0f78d38a0368\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":89027},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"89d78d15-6129-443f-85f0-8fb43f3be778\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:18:06.752Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"89d78d15-6129-443f-85f0-8fb43f3be778\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d20d237c10e16c2a1c7daaa87f6c3\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The Python simulation had a bug (setting mask bits for 'X'). The corrected pattern needs `'0'` at char[7]