- bit 34\\n\\nSo in gem5, the THUMB and AARCH64 flags are NOT bit 5 and bit 4 of CPSR as in real ARM hardware. Instead, they are separate constructed bitfields in the 64-bit ExtMachInst:\\n- `thumb` = bit 36\\n- `bigThumb` = bit 35\\n- `aarch64` = bit 34\\n\\n\\nThe decoder uses these ExtMachInst fields rather than the CPSR directly. I need to trace back where ExtMachInst gets constructed from the incoming instruction stream and how these bitfields are actually populated based on the execution state.\",\"signature\":\"3a45a4f242beb42b787703661be60475a465abb7c5782be1eda5203ae31e9c72\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":218,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":703,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":45274},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"657574be-8975-4d94-876d-559e2df48222\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:37:14.747Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"657574be-8975-4d94-876d-559e2df48222\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d3384a46094fa61aa1481ae851965\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Now I understand the architecture. THUMB is bit 36, AARCH64 is bit 34 of ExtMachInst. Let me find where the decoder's THUMB/AARCH64 switches get their values - they must be defined somewhere.\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":218,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":703,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":45274},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"cea9ec61-00b6-459d-8c3e-c9081944fc66\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:37:16.080Z\",\"userType\":\"external