t elements (double-precision) → FmlaDX/FmlaQX\\n- size=3: reserved\\n\\nBut I don't distinguish FMLA from FMLS. \\n\\nLooking at how the actual NEON decoder handles these instructions, it uses `decodeNeonUThreeFpReg` which delegates to either `FmlaDX` or `FmlsDX` based on the opcode. I need to extract the opcode bits and map them to the correct instruction variant instead of just using size.\\n\\nLet me reconsider the FMLS instruction encoding more carefully. The opcode bits 15:10 are 011011, so I need to verify whether that matches the FMLA encoding and how to properly distinguish between these instructions based on the full opcode field. I need to handle both FMLA and FMLS cases, so I'll decode the opcode field and switch on it—FMLA (0x19) and FMLS (0x1B) each dispatch to their respective instruction classes with the correct type parameters, while invalid opcodes return unknown.\",\"signature\":\"f285d45a7c70105065eb238fb00059d99ae6ebdbac71e3f6a29ec0daa60c70ae\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":818,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":93215},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"2f1f7ea9-127f-4ef3-9bbf-4e96fb6001b1\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T02:51:29.053Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"2f1f7ea9-127f-4ef3-9bbf-4e96fb6001b1\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d0ca5e966b6290a0babd93a8f597f\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Wait, I need to distinguish FMLA vs FMLS. Let me check what class names to use and fix the implementation.\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":n