596:53: note: expression evaluates to '21 == 20'\\n  596 |     static_assert(msb >= 0 && lsb >= 0 && msb - lsb == sizeof...(rest));\\n      |                                           ~~~~~~~~~~^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\\n1 error generated.\\nscons: *** [build/ARM/arch/arm/generated/inst-constrs-3.o] Error 1\\nscons: building terminated because of errors.\\n*** Summary of Warnings ***\\nWarning: You can get a 12% performance improvement by installing tcmalloc\\n         (libgoogle-perftools-dev package on Ubuntu or RedHat).\\nWarning: Header file <capstone/capstone.h> not found.\\n         This host has no capstone library installed.\\nWarning: Info: Compatible header file <linux/kvm.h> not found, disabling KVM\\n         support.\\nWarning: Header file <png.h> not found.\\n         This host has no libpng library.\\n         Disabling support for PNG framebuffers.\\nWarning: Can't find library for POSIX clocks.\\nWarning: Couldn't find HDF5 C++ libraries. Disabling HDF5 support.\\nWarning: Cannot enable KVM, host seems to lack KVM support\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"uuid\":\"95b65823-7769-431a-b89f-d075eb7fdd4d\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T02:54:30.247Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"5a09200f-33d1-4a7b-9c18-67ed82e2a32c\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"95b65823-7769-431a-b89f-d075eb7fdd4d\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d0d66595c3394d29f42e2b9aa0b46\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"The error says: `31 - 10 == 21 == sizeof...(rest)` but I only have 20 characters. Let me count the characters I used:\\n\\n```\\n'0','0','0','1', // op0: bits31:28=0001\\n'1','1','1',      // (3)\\n'0','0',         // op1: bits24:23=00 (2)\\n'X','X','X','X', // op2: bits22:19=XXXX (4)\\n'X','X','1','X', // op3: bits15=1, rest X (4)\\n\\n\\n'X','X','X','X'  // op3 continued (4)\\n```\\n\\nThat's 4 + 3 + 2 + 4 + 4 + 4 = 21 characters. But the compiler says I have 20. Let me recount the bit positions more carefully. For a 32-bit instruction starting at bit 31 and ending at bit 10, that's 22 bits total, so I need 22 template parameters, not 21.\\n\\nLet me verify the pattern breakdown: bits 31-28 give me 4 chars, bits 27-25 give me 3 chars, bits 24-23 give me 2 chars, bits 22-19 give me 4 chars, and bits 18-10 give me 9 chars. Adding those up: 4 + 3 + 2 + 4 + 9 = 22. So I need 22 characters total to match the 22 bits in that range.\\n\\nNow I'm mapping out the bit positions for the FMLA/FMLS instruction, where bits 15 and 14 are fixed at 1, and bits 13-10 are don't-cares.\\n\\nI need 9 total bit specifiers for the 18-10 range, so I'm adding four more 'X' placeholders to complete the pattern. I'm filling in the remaining bits from position 10 up to 18 with X placeholders to complete the 22-character sequence, then verifying the full instruction layout matches the expected bit positions. I see the issue now—I need exactly 22 character specifiers to match the 22 bits between positions 31 and 10. Let me recalculate: bits 31-28 give me 4 characters, 27-25 give me 3, 24-23 give me 2, 22-19 give me 4, and 18-10 give me 9, which totals 22. I had only included 17 characters instead of the required 22, which is why the pattern wasn't matching correctly. I see the issue now—I'm missing two more 'X' placeholders in the third row. Let me recount the character positions: the first row has 4 characters for op0, the second row has 3 for op1, the third row has 4 for op2, and I need 4 more for the bit positions 18-15 before starting on op3. That gives me 17 total, but I need 22 positions for bits 31-10, so I'm still 5 characters short in my pattern definition. I'm recounting the character positions across the bit ranges to figure out where th