ated headers. The extern template declarations are telling the compiler these specializations exist in another translation unit, so they should be defined somewhere in the object files. Let me search the exec-ns.cc.inc file more carefully for where these definitions are actually instantiated. I'm realizing the mismatch: `FmlsDX<uint16_t>` should map to a D-register with 128 bits total, which means 8 half-precision elements across 4 registers, but the template specialization at line 247840 with `rCount=2` only allocates space for 4 elements total. Let me trace through the actual register layout to see where the discrepancy is.\\n\\nActually, looking at how `AA64FpOp1` is declared as a `VecRegContainer` with underlying uint32_t array—that's 4 uint32_t lanes giving 512 bits total, which is way more than a single D-register needs. I think the real issue is that the `template` declaration on line 247971 is just an explicit instantiation declaration, meaning the actual template definition for `FmlsDX<uint16_t>::execute` must be generated elsewhere in the file. Let me search more systematically for where this definition actually appears.\",\"signature\":\"a4913c39172bec5d55f78228726223159099b0721ec1c4fc01dcc93e8b8159d9\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1284,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":69987},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"afbc67b8-e9b2-45a5-9bdc-5a2310266411\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:07:00.384Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"afbc67b8-e9b2-45a5-9bdc-5a2310266411\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d1e5419015834621afa9a9609f9f2\",\"type\":\"m