 you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"uuid\":\"49554d86-f891-439d-bb1f-c504fe177fdf\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:48:55.931Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"a37ecb68-306c-4a78-af7d-ee3d40eaac34\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"49554d86-f891-439d-bb1f-c504fe177fdf\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d2838af8ef2cb51a88e2ecef80c53\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"`decoder.cc` includes `decoder-g.cc.inc` (NOT `decoder-ns.cc.inc`!). And `decode-method.cc.inc` has the `ArmISA::Decoder::decodeInst` function.\\n\\nSo `decoder-ns.cc.inc` IS included somewhere - probably in the `.o` files via the `inst-constrs-*.cc` files.\\n\\nBut `decoder.cc` does NOT include `decoder-ns.cc.inc`. So the patterns and `decodeFpAdvSIMD` definitions from `decoder-ns.cc.inc` are NOT available in `decoder.cc`.\\n \\nWait, I need to reconsider how the compilation actually works. The `inst-constrs-*.cc` files are compiled into separate object files and then linked together into `gem5.opt`, so even though `decoder.cc` doesn't directly include `decoder-ns.cc.inc`, the symbol definitions from `inst-constrs-*.cc` should still be available at link time.\\n\\nThe linker should be able to find `decodeFpAdvSIMD` from the compiled `inst-constrs-*.o` files, but the disassembly of `decodeFpAdvSIMD` shows it never calls my `decodeFpMulMadd` function, which means the old version without my changes must still be compiled into the binary. This could be a caching issue where the build system isn't detecting that the `.isa` source file has