,\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"76dd6c29-2458-48f1-8f26-534dd1020b3e\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d284b0dd18e106ad2d4482db03ade\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"The debug string IS in the binary. But `decodeFpAdvSIMD` is not being called at runtime. Why?\\n\\nLet me think about this differently. `decodeFpAdvSIMD` is in the `Aarch64` namespace. But `decodeInst` (in `ArmISA::Decoder`) calls it via `using namespace Aarch64;`. Maybe there's a different decode path for AtomicSimpleCPU.\\n\\nWait - what if the actual decode call uses a different template of `decodeFpAdvSIMD`? Like `decodeFpAdvSIMD<SomeOtherDecoder>` instead of `decodeFpAdvSIMD<GenericDecoder>`? The debug statement would only fire for the template that I modified.\\n \\nI need to figure out which decoder template is actually being used at runtime - there might be multiple instantiations like `decodeFpAdvSIMD<GenericDecoder>` versus something else entirely, and my debug output only covers one of them.\",\"signature\":\"3fc277f170dbb4a38e59b808391fd8eb14ab7095493e190204ff948183fe0c92\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":162,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":142981},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"857f120c-450e-4241-a6b7-518b62b690f6\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:49:24.174Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"857f120c-450e-4241-a6b7-518b62b690f6\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d284b0dd18e106ad2d4482db03ade\",\"type\":\"messag