 check for `bits27:25=111` comes after several other conditions, so one of those earlier branches must be matching first and returning a different handler.\\n\\nLet me work through the bit analysis for the instruction: bits 27-25 are all 1, and bit 26 is also 1, which means the `if (bits(machInst, 26) == 0)` check fails, so execution should reach the final `else` clause where I return the `decodeFpAdvSIMD` handler. bit 25 is 1, so this check also fails. Since bit 24 is 0, not 1, the third condition fails too, which means we correctly fall through to the final else block and return `decodeFpAdvSIMD`. But the debug output isn't appearing, which suggests either the build didn't actually use the new binary, scons ran from a different directory than expected, or the object files weren't rebuilt despite the source changes.\\n\\nLet me verify by touching the file to force a rebuild and checking the resulting binary with objdump.\",\"signature\":\"e07d0ccaad038197315098b5647271e11d96cc35a1442dbae5da82838c0e757f\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":8,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":145144},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"32a46dc9-3445-491d-8f32-99538e885df3\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:50:56.296Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"32a46dc9-3445-491d-8f32-99538e885df3\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d28a13f3de0ec176859754568d024\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me verify the debug is actually in the compiled binary code:\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequenc