",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:09:55.055Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"2095ab9e-0102-4c0a-9061-efdc4b76f58e\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"240c88ae-a16d-4841-b1a4-e98984ab9015\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d2d23786612a5d060ff57702cc947\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Still no debug output! But I verified the binary has the debug string... Wait, the backtrace showed the panic is from `UndefinedInstruction::invoke` being called from `advancePC`. This means the instruction WAS decoded successfully (returning an `Unknown64` StaticInst), but then when the CPU tried to execute it, `UndefinedInstruction::invoke` was called.\\n\\nLet me trace back: the `Unknown64::execute` method calls `std::make_shared<UndefinedInstruction>(machInst, true)`. This creates an `UndefinedInstruction` fault. Then the fault is returned from execute. The CPU handles the fault and calls `UndefinedInstruction::invoke`, which panics.\\n \\nI added debug output to `Unknown64::execute` in the misc64.isa file, and the string is in the binary, but it's not printing. Let me verify the binary actually contains the compiled code that prints the debug message before creating the fault.\",\"signature\":\"2e9224b892650e84cbe965f280f20875e73ec92ba221bea86d882c9e9f958b1d\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":218,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":263,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":140293},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"5762d462-cc81-4e19-acb8-b85fe25d6bf2\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:10:03.107Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"