8 start + 6076\\n--- END LIBC BACKTRACE ---\\nFor more info on how to address this issue, please visit https://www.gem5.org/documentation/general_docs/common-errors/\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"uuid\":\"3e6929d3-2d4a-4223-9c7a-cf96a45442f6\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:59:59.284Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"f10c90a4-5a2e-4be6-9760-4e9449c50c41\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"3e6929d3-2d4a-4223-9c7a-cf96a45442f6\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d1cbf736192241f3542a3050eb73e\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"The error is `UndefinedInstruction` (line 6: `REDACTED`). This is an `UndefinedInstruction` exception, which is different from an \\\"unknown instruction\\\" panic. An `UndefinedInstruction` means the decode DID succeed (an instruction object was created), but the CPU tried to execute it and it raised an undefined instruction exception.\\n\\nThis is actually progress! The decode is working - it's no longer returning `Unknown64`. Instead, it's returning some instruction that triggers an `UndefinedInstruction` exception at execution time.\\n\\n\\nThe issue is that `FmlsDX` inherits from a base class that marks it as requiring the `FPLS` or floating-point feature flag, so when the CPU doesn't have that flag set, it throws an undefined instruction exception at runtime rather than during decoding.\\n\\nThe real problem might be that the instruction encoding I'm generating isn't matching what gem5 expects for this CPU type—gem5's `UndefinedInstruction` could be firing because the instruction IS technically defined but triggers a condition that makes it undefined in this context, like an invalid register encoding or operand combination. Looking at the stack trace, the crash happens during execution when `advancePC` is called after an undefined instruction exception, not during decoding itself. So the instruction was decoded successfully, but when the CPU tries to execute it, gem5 throws an undefined instruction exception. This means either the instruction requires a feature or extension that's not enabled in my config, or gem5's implementation of these instructions treats them as undefined on this particular CPU model.\\n\\nThe real issue is likely that gem5 checks whether the FPLS extension (which includes FMLS and FMLA) is available on the CPU, and since I'm using AtomicSimpleCPU with minimal configuration, that extension probably isn't enabled, causing the exception to fire when the instruction attempts to execute. I should verify the ARM architecture extensions available in my configuration and check gem5's source code to understand how it validates floating-point instruction availability at runtime.\",\"signature\":\"5c3850f9c8cb54aef054942f68d158cd7804722b6ccc20d33de236d5fbbee81b\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1318,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":42781},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"bf278a40-ffc0-42ee-85f9-aa43867161a6\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:00:15.187Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"bf278a40-ffc0-42ee-85f9-aa43867161a6\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d1cbf736192241f3542a3050eb73e\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The error changed - now it's `UndefinedInstruction` at **execution time** (not decode time). This means the decode IS working (returning an instruction object), but gem5 throws an undefined-instruction exception when trying to execute it. This likely means the FMLS instruction requires a floating-point extension that isn't enabled in our CPU config.\\n\\nLet me investigate:\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1318,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":42781},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"718b4e61-0011-4858-a094-fddf51a2d1c4\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:00:16.928Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"718b4e61-0011-4858-a094-fddf51a2d1c4\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d1cbf736192241f3542a3050eb73e\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_function_gar7ka4s0ob3_1\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"UndefinedInstruction\\\\|FML.*undef\\\\|FP.*undef\\\\|checkFPEnabled\\\\|fpEnabled\\\\|haveFP\\\\|FPLS\\\\|ArmExtension\\\" /Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5/src/arch/arm/isa/insts/neon64.isa 2>/dev/null | head -30\"}}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1318,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":42781},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"95b115f4-0473-4029-ab56-e86742bdde31\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:00:19.770Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\