ch gives 0x5e288000, and the AND operation against the instruction bits isolates those same bits for comparison.\\n\\nLooking at the generated code structure, each bitPatternMatcher in the generated decoder maps to a specific mask-and-match constant pair, so I need to identify which pattern constant corresponds to the FMLS instruction in the actual disassembly. Rather than tracing through all the comparison instructions, I should just disassemble the `decodeFpMulMadd` function directly to see what's actually happening.\",\"signature\":\"ab2b3252affe831f8b676eef2e96aa197b7ae11d40128b9da35159d286271ed2\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2561,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":113295},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"8ebe1a6e-98e1-4b31-9299-c23c5cd31a68\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:34:24.695Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"8ebe1a6e-98e1-4b31-9299-c23c5cd31a68\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d24af8b02e8efbee41ef09d6e9373\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me disassemble `decodeFpMulMadd` to verify the binary has the correct logic:\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2561,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":113295},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"973aa8bf-7430-405f-8e9d-c6e5620c47db\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:34:25.160Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"s