d `decodeFpAdvSIMD` definitions from `decoder-ns.cc.inc` are NOT available in `decoder.cc`.\\n \\nWait, I need to reconsider how the compilation actually works. The `inst-constrs-*.cc` files are compiled into separate object files and then linked together into `gem5.opt`, so even though `decoder.cc` doesn't directly include `decoder-ns.cc.inc`, the symbol definitions from `inst-constrs-*.cc` should still be available at link time.\\n\\nThe linker should be able to find `decodeFpAdvSIMD` from the compiled `inst-constrs-*.o` files, but the disassembly of `decodeFpAdvSIMD` shows it never calls my `decodeFpMulMadd` function, which means the old version without my changes must still be compiled into the binary. This could be a caching issue where the build system isn't detecting that the `.isa` source file has changed and recompiling the affected files. I'm looking at the object files to verify whether they're compiled from the `.isa` source or cached versions.\",\"signature\":\"5ab8383bcda914c54035e04ed5a9fc88e41171625c8d97f92fbe316db38c40f2\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":341,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":142056},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"dbf0487e-ac3e-452b-a3d0-db32b9032263\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:49:04.594Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"dbf0487e-ac3e-452b-a3d0-db32b9032263\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d2838af8ef2cb51a88e2ecef80c53\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me check if the object files are stale:\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":nul