tch default! And line 2925: `return new Unknown(machInst)` - this returns `Unknown`, not `Unknown64`!Wait, this is in the generated `decode-method.cc.inc`, NOT in the `Aarch64::` namespace. This is `ArmISA::Decoder::decodeInst`, which returns `Unknown` (not `Unknown64`). And `Unknown` is defined as `class Unknown : public ArmStaticInst`.So the path IS:\\n1. `ArmISA::Decoder::decodeInst`2. Switch case THUMB=0 (AARCH64 is 1)3. Switch case AARCH64=1 (since bit34=1 of emi)4. \\n\\nNow I see the issue - the AARCH64 switch has a default case that returns an `Unknown` instruction instead of continuing through the thumb path. The problem is that THUMB is set to 0 for AArch64 instructions, which routes them through the AARCH64=1 case where they hit this default return rather than being properly decoded. I need to check how the THUMB field is actually defined in the types and whether AArch64 instructions should even be going through this path at all.\",\"signature\":\"aa33165d52272a650bd8af3b9a0d191b5d324b1ad199b86c927f457523cc2b27\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":520,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":153697},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"7dcfc2ba-8ddb-46f2-a71b-a5fa59478da0\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:56:48.178Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"7dcfc2ba-8ddb-46f2-a71b-a5fa59478da0\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d2a0585f137d35de3df3c19f0829e\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Found it! Line 2922: `default:` - AARCH64=1 falls through to `return new Unknown(machInst)`! The AARCH64 bit must