":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"So at line 174, `emi.aarch64 = pc.aarch64()`. The `pc.aarch64()` method reads from the PCState. In gem5, the PCState for ARM has an `aarch64` flag that indicates whether the CPU is in AArch64 mode.\\n\\nFor a bare-metal ARM64 ELF, the CPU should be in AArch64 mode. But something is setting it to 0 (AArch32).\\n\\nLet me check the PCState definition for ARM to understand how `aarch64()` works.\",\"signature\":\"771505e24990c7256a318bc5192ccf4b50f71505f5267cccffa8c4d8ab0e11a4\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":69019},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"9eefa74f-deb0-41bf-b34f-989f3c59f932\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:44:44.692Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"9eefa74f-deb0-41bf-b34f-989f3c59f932\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d3547aab2c7e0ecb66921158704db\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_function_syu418k37d4d_1\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"grep -rn \\\"aarch64\\\\|thumb\\\\|debugStep\\\" /Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5/src/arch/arm/pcstate.hh 2>/dev/null | head -30\",\"description\":\"Find PCState aarch64/thumb methods\"}}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":69019,\"output_tokens\":201,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_5m_input