how the decoder is getting AARCH64=0.\\n\\nLet me check how the PC flags are initialized. When the workload starts, who sets the AArch64 flag?\\n\\nLooking at the `moreBytes` method in decoder.cc:\\n```cpp\\nemi.thumb = pc.thumb();\\nemi.aarch64 = pc.aarch64();\\n\\n\\n```\\n\\nSo `emi.aarch64` is set from `pc.aarch64()`. And `pc.aarch64()` returns `(flags & AArch64Bit) != 0`. If this returns 0, then either the flag isn't set in the PC or something else is clearing it. I need to trace where the PC flags get initialized—likely in `SEWorkload::initState()` or wherever the PC is first set up for bare-metal execution. Let me check how the AARCH64 flag gets propagated through the bitfields in types.hh, since `emi.aarch64` is defined there and the decode switch relies on it.\\n\\n```\",\"signature\":\"7be07be852a50728308a72417fa5c352272194f3d19b997702f58d67a3cf880b\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":218,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":435,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":70121},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"3448b28b-ee87-4f2a-9291-ed59ddcc8a9b\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:45:04.865Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"3448b28b-ee87-4f2a-9291-ed59ddcc8a9b\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d3557230c30549bb35498678e711b\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"\\nThe PC's AArch64 flag depends on `flags & 0x4`. Let me check how the PC flags are initialized when the bare-metal workload starts.\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":218,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation