and FADD/FSUB I need to account for the full opcode encoding across multiple bit positions. Let me trace through the actual instruction encoding to see exactly which bits differentiate these operations. Now I'm seeing the pattern—FMLS uses the same opcode as FSUB, which means the top-level decoder can't distinguish between them, but FMLA has a unique opcode that separates it from FADD. The encoding space shows FMUL and FMLA are distinct, FADD and FMSUB are distinct, while FMLS gets confused with FSUB, and FNMSUB with FNADD. FNADD doesn't exist in the architecture, so this overlap might not cause practical issues.\\n\\nNow I need to focus on the actual problem: FMLA is routing to the wrong decode function and returning an incorrect result. I'm modifying the top-level decoder pattern and updating the switch statement in `decodeFpDataProc2Source` to check the full opcode field and properly distinguish FMLA/FMLS from their FSUB counterparts.\\n\\nUpdating the switch cases...\",\"signature\":\"052a932f7879bdfb241d33563d7496a9783c457cf6a630dadbc23d2484d44997\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":492,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":65200},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"a08f1118-0168-4632-828c-06d7f23f32f6\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T02:36:00.797Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"a08f1118-0168-4632-828c-06d7f23f32f6\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d08fedcb930cb41bcf6ec9cf481c8\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Found the root cause. `0x1e2e1000` = FMLA Sd, Sn, Sm, with `switchVal=0x02` which maps to