 scalar case, I need to extract the U bit and opcode from the instruction encoding to route correctly between these two operations. I see that `decodeNeonUThreeFpReg` handles the dispatch for FMLA and FMLS based on the U bit, so I need to verify whether this same function works for scalar forms or if I need a separate decoder. Let me check how scalar FMUL is currently handled in `decodeFpDataProc2Source` to understand the pattern for scalar floating-point operations.\\n\\nActually, I'm realizing the real issue here: when bit21=1 in the FMLS encoding, it incorrectly matches the `isFpDataProc2Source` pattern, causing the instruction to be dispatched to the wrong decoder. The solution is to catch FMLA/FMLS instructions with a dedicated pattern that recognizes the bit21=1 condition, then route them to the correct NEON decoder that can properly handle scalar forms. I need to verify what instruction classes are actually available in the neon64 templates to properly handle the scalar floating-point multiply-accumulate operations.\",\"signature\":\"82e9f67aa8237c22e9afdc5836b47d91df828fbf9c298d3947cffda2660a2606\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":80990},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"e40129de-b16b-413b-b0c2-bf815088b3f7\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T02:43:33.609Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"e40129de-b16b-413b-b0c2-bf815088b3f7\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d0ac3a0f6f27b1121d6a2bc191822\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Good - `FmlaDX`/`FmlaQX`/`FmlsDX`/`FmlsQ