\")  \\nprint(f\\\"bit25    = 0x{bit25:x}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"bit24:23 = 0x{bit24_23:x}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"bit22:19 = 0x{bit22_19:x}\\\")\\n\\nok_op0 = ((bit31_28 >> 3) & 1) == 0  # bit31=0\\nok_op1_bit1 = (bit27_26 >> 1) == 1   # bit27=1\\nok_op1_bit0 = (bit27_26 & 1) == 1    # bit26=1\\nok_op1_bit24 = (bit24_23 >> 1) == 0   # bit24=0\\nok_op1_bit23 = (bit24_23 & 1) == 0   # bit23=0\\nok_op2_bit22 = (bit22_19 >> 3) == 1  # bit22=1\\n\\nprint(f\\\"\\\\nisConvFloatPFixedP checks:\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"  op0: bit31=0: {ok_op0}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"  op1: bit27=1: {ok_op1_bit1}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"  op1: bit26=1: {ok_op1_bit1}\\\")  \\nprint(f\\\"  op1: bit24=0: {ok_op1_bit24}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"  op1: bit23=0: {ok_op1_bit23}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"  op2: bit22=1: {ok_op2_bit22}\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"\\\\nNEW isConvFloatPFixedP MATCH: {ok_op0 and ok_op1_bit1 and ok_op1_bit24 and ok_op1_bit23 and ok_op2_bit22}\\\")\\n\\n# Also verify: what instructions DOES this break?\\n# FCVT Fixed->FP: bit22=1, bit24=0, bit23=0\\n# FMLA/FMLS: bit22=1, bit24=0, bit23=0, bit21=1\\n# These were previously both matching isConvFloatPFixedP, but only FCVT should.\\n# After the fix: both still match (since bit21 is wild). But the opcode check in\\n# decodeFpConvFixed should reject FMLA/FMLS.\\nprint(f\\\"\\\\n=> Both FCVT and FMLA would still match isConvFloatPFixedP.\\\")\\nprint(f\\\"=> decodeFpConvFixed must distinguish them by opcode.\\\")\\nPYEOF\",\"description\":\"Verify isConvFloatPFixedP change rejects FMLA/FMLS\"}}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":131262,\"output_tokens\":869,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"71da5b60-2f66-428b-b1c0-b4200f7c8c2f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:17:36.485Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"71da5b60-2f66-428b-b1c0-b4200f7c8c2f\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"520da623-e17e-4efe-b292-47222de157e3\",\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_function_fpsd0j3q24pa_1\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"bit31:28 = 0x1\\nbit27:26 = 0x3\\nbit25    = 0x1\\nbit24:23 = 0x0\\nbit22:19 = 0x5\\n\\nisConvFloatPFixedP checks:\\n  op0: bit31=0: True\\n  op1: bit27=1: True\\n  op1: bit26=1: True\\n  op1: bit24=0: True\\n  op1: bit23=0: True\\n  op2: bit22=1: False\\n\\nNEW isConvFloatPFixedP MATCH: False\\n\\n=> Both FCVT and FMLA would still match isConvFloatPFixedP.\\n=> decodeFpConvFixed must distinguish them by opcode.\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"uuid\":\"559e632e-e1f5-4748-8b95-660efb6a7db1\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:17:36.621Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"71da5b60-2f66-428b-b1c0-b4200f7c8c2f\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"559e632e-e1f5-4748-8b95-660efb6a7db1\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d12d1447c29362707748dc559040b\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"The `isConvFloatPFixedP` change correctly rejects FMLA/FMLS (bit22=1 in the instruction, but the pattern requires bit22=0 → doesn't match). Wait, I set `'1','X','X','X'` at the op2 position which maps to bits 22:19. Let me re-check what the pattern maps to.\\n\\n`bitPatternMatcher<MachInst, 31, 10>`:\\n- First group: bits 31:28\\n- Second group: bits 27:25\\n- Third group: bits 24:23\\n- Fourth group: bits 22:19\\n- Fifth group: bits 18:15\\n\\n\\n- Sixth group: bits 14:10\\n\\nSo the groups are: 'X','0','X','1' for bits 31:28, '1','1','1' for bits 27:25, '0','0' for bits 24:23, '1','X','X','X' for bits 22:19, 'X','X','X','X','X' for bits 18:15, and the last group for bits 14:10.\\n\\nFor the instruction 0x1e2e1000, I'm checking what bits 22:19 are. They're 0101 in binary, so bit 22 is 0. The pattern requires this bit to be 1, so this instruction doesn't match. With the new pattern, `isConvFloatPFixedP` won't catch FMLA/FMLS anymore since it requires bit 22=1, which those instructions don't have. That means they'll correctly route to `isFpMulMadd` instead.\\n\\nNow I'm checking whether FCVT instructions still work. For SCVTF Dd, Xn, #fbits, I need to verify that bit 22=1, which it should be for this instruction. Let me verify the bit positions in the encoding—the rmode field is at bits 20:19 and type is at bit 21, so the original pattern's `'0','X','X','X'` constraint correctly enforces type=0 for the scalar FP conversion instructions. Since my modification changes op2 to `'1','X','X','X'`, requiring type=1 instead, I need to verify this still works for the FCVTZS and FCVTZU variants.\\n\\nActually, I realize the SCVTF encoding has type=0 at bit 21, so requiring bit 22=1 would exclude it entirely. Let me reconsider whether the constraint should be applied differently—perhaps bit 21 should be 0 to distinguish from other instruction classes, but I need to think through which specific instructions should be caught by this pattern. I'm realizing the original pattern already handled this correctly—all FCVTZS and FCVTZU variants match `isConvFloatPFixedP` regardless of bit 21, and they all route to the same decoder which handles them all with the type check. The issue was that FMLA and FMLS shouldn't have matched this pattern in the first place, but they did because bit 22 wasn't constrained, and the decoder would eventually reject them with an opcode mismatch. I'm realizing my change might have unintended consequences for other instruction classes. Let me think through whether SCVTF and related instructions would still match with the new constraint—bit 22 is already 1 for those cases, so they should be fine, but I need to verify this doesn't break anything else downstream. I see the issue now—I need to check the constraint on bit 21 to properly distinguish between FCVTZS/U and FMLA/FMLS. For FCVTZS/U, bit 21 should be 0, but for FMLA/FMLS it's 1, so setting `bit21 = '0'` in the pattern will correctly exclude the FMLA/FMLS instructions while keeping the fixed-point conversion instructions.\\n\\nNow I need to update the pattern in aarch64.isa and then verify that both FCVTZS Dd, Xn, #fbits and FCVTZU Dd, Xn, #fbits will still match the corrected pattern.\\n\\nVerifying the bit patterns... I'm seeing that my earlier fix was actually working correctly—bit22 needs to be 1 for FCVT instructions, which is already the case, so changing the constraint from 'X' to '1' for bit22 won't affect those instructions. But I made a mistake by also requiring bit27 and bit26 to be 1 when they should be 0 instead. Let me look at the actual pattern definition again to see what I changed.\",\"signature\":\"74812a87c6d832d968d408aa5c882e7345dcff48b8a542702ad1941caa9c2040\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":341,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":131707},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"f4270198-0b2b-4ea9-aa55-2828f8ed9dd0\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:18:05.675Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1