nfirmed that `decodeInst` IS called with the correct machInst. And the panic happens in `UndefinedInstruction::invoke`. \\n\\nWait, let me reconsider. Looking at the stack trace:\\n```0   gem5.opt                            0x0000000100002b7c REDACTED + 0\\n\\n\\n1   gem5.opt                            0x00000001005195d8 REDACTED + 248\\n```\\n\\nThe `UndefinedInstruction::invoke` at 0x00000001005195d8 calls `onUDelay` at 0x0000000100002b7c. So `onUDelay` is inside `UndefinedInstruction::invoke`. The debug I added to `decodeFpAdvSIMD` isn't being reached, which suggests the unknown instruction path isn't being triggered through the decoder.\\n\\nActually, let me think about the stack trace more carefully. In a backtrace, each frame shows the return address - the address the function returns TO. So frame 0 is `onUDelay`, which means `UndefinedInstruction::invoke` called `onUDelay` and the crash happened inside `onUDelay`. Frame 1 shows `UndefinedInstruction::invoke` itself. So the actual crash location is inside `onUDelay`, but it's being called from within `UndefinedInstruction::invoke`.\\n\\nNow I need to figure out what `onUDelay` is actually doing and whether the `decodeInst` debug message I added is reaching the output stream.\\n\\nLooking at the backtrace again, I notice the top frame is `onUDelay` at 0x0000000100002b7c - this is called FROM `UndefinedInstruction::invoke` at frame 1. So the panic is happening inside `UndefinedInstruction::invoke` when it tries to execute the instruction.\\n\\nBut here's the puzzle: my `decodeInst` debug print confirms the instruction is being decoded, yet neither the \\\"Unknown path\\\" debug nor the `decodeFpAdvSIMD` debug is showing up. This suggests either the debug output isn't being flushed before the panic occurs, or the instruction is being decoded through a completely different code path than I'm expecting.\\n\\nLet me search through the generated decoder code to find where `Unknown(machInst)` is actually being returned, since that's what the \\\"Unknown path\\\" debug would be triggered from.\",\"signature\":\"ae9ffe3ddce958830c916cfaad36d61162b8e6981fce067ec09e8bfb7c183348\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":217,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":155566},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"71fab1fc-1809-4a63-9185-22dca2a7fa8a\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:59:06.008Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"71fab1fc-1809-4a63-9185-22dca2a7fa8a\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d2a87ec4795d00441da832836f41e\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me search all places that return `Unknown` or `Unknown64`:\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":217,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":155566},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"52c8ae30-5d60-4e05-a0a7-7511a8776076\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:59:06.467Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"52c8ae30-5d60-4e05-a0a7-7511a8776076\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d2a87ec4795d00441da832836f41e\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_function_26bwj1aujv4h_1\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"