r entirely, so the destination starts as zero, whereas FmlaDX with `readDest=True` would preserve the original destination value. That's why the outputs are different. I'm tracing through how the FmlsDX execute method actually works—the declaration exists but the definition doesn't seem to be where I expected it in the generated file, so I need to search more carefully through the exec_output to find where it's actually being instantiated. me think about this differently. The `exec_output` from the ISA compiler gets written to exec-ns.cc.inc. For template classes, the compiler generates the template instantiations. The template itself should be in the exec-ns.cc.inc.\\n\\nLet me search for the template definition of `FmlsDX` execute.\\n\\nActually wait - I just realized something. Let me look at the broader context. The `Fault FmlsDX<uint16_t>::execute` at line 247972 is a declaration. And looking at line 247979-24801, `FmlsQX<Element>::execute` has a full definition. So `FmlsQX` is fully defined. But `FmlsDX` only has declarations.\\n\\nThis is suspicious. Let me check if there's a conditional compilation or if the definitions are elsewhere in the exec output. Maybe the `FmlsDX` definitions got placed in a different exec file.\",\"signature\":\"d09601bc9c3086ff1cbc0aca5e455062340eccc19019fe3a2b9b59227751a246\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1407,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":64274},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"f189eb0c-4dba-45b3-8154-1a04af7bc224\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:05:21.774Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"f189eb0c-4dba-45b3-8154-1a04af7bc224\",\"isSidechain\":tru