tted version with the instruction bytes.\\n\\nThe backtrace shows this is coming through `UndefinedInstruction::invoke` rather than the normal instruction execution path, which suggests the instruction isn't being decoded at all—it's being caught by the illegal execution fault path. Let me trace back through the fetch and decode logic to see where the actual decoding happens and why this instruction is triggering a fault instead.\\n\\nNow I'm noticing the backtrace shows `advancePC` calling `UndefinedInstruction::invoke` during `AtomicSimpleCPU::tick`, which means the instruction is successfully decoding to some `StaticInstPtr`, but that instruction is then throwing an exception when it executes. I need to check what `advancePC` is doing—it's likely catching a fault and handling the PC advancement, but I should verify the exact flow to understand why the decode succeeded but execution is failing.\",\"signature\":\"48ce6f477b901eb2032b07e014b4c7ccb24e717480b257cf4dbe5a8b56134d48\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":416,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":147465},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"1bfeaf08-d76d-4385-82a2-32bc633f6be0\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:53:10.578Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"1bfeaf08-d76d-4385-82a2-32bc633f6be0\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d2927233086e9e9891db00149a89c\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The debug proves `decodeFpAdvSIMD` is never called. The instruction must be intercepted somewhere earlier. Let me add debug to the top-level `decodeInst` in t