rsion\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"7b652e37-b22e-4df0-8fbb-f99c779e0b51\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"520da623-e17e-4efe-b292-47222de157e3\",\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_function_mlofxsq0zkj4_1\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"(Bash completed with no output)\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"uuid\":\"3e2512a1-e40b-439a-925e-0e95157c85fa\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:08:16.090Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"7b652e37-b22e-4df0-8fbb-f99c779e0b51\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"3e2512a1-e40b-439a-925e-0e95157c85fa\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d2cc058dcdeb4958ea7539dd99af9\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"The file was regenerated WITHOUT my debug edits. The file timestamp is 13:02. My edit to the generated file was done before, and the scons build must have regenerated it.\\n\\nSo the current file does NOT have the debug. And the binary does NOT have the debug prints either (because `DEBUG decodeFpAdvSIMD` is NOT in the binary - it's from `decoder-ns.cc.inc`).\\n\\nThe issue is: the decode-method.cc.inc is regenerated by scons every time, but it doesn't include the debug from decoder-ns.cc.inc because `decodeFpAdvSIMD` is defined in decoder-ns.cc.inc (in namespace `Aarch64`), not in decode-method.cc.inc.\\n \\nNow I see the actual flow: `decodeInst` calls `decodeFpAdvSIMD`, which is defined in decoder-ns.cc.inc and contains the debug output. But when I run the test, the debug doesn't print and instead I get an Unknown panic. The problem is that `decodeInst` is returning an Unknown instruction without ever invoking `decodeFpAdvSIMD`. Looking at the decode tree, I'm trying to trace through which case is actually being hit for the FMLS instruction.\\n\\nFor FMLS at 0x1e2e1000, the instruction has THUMB=0, AARCH64=1, and bits27:25=111, which should route through the FP/AdvSIMD path. But the debug shows that AARCH64 is being read as 0 instead of 1, which means the switch is taking the wrong branch and falling through to the default case that returns Unknown.\\n\\nThe real question is why the bit extraction is giving me 0 when the instruction encoding clearly shows AARCH64 should be 1. If the AARCH64 field is actually 0, then the instruction would be interpreted as ARM state instead of AArch64, which would explain why the decoder is rejecting it as unknown. I'm looking at the bitfield extraction logic in the BitUnion implementation, which uses `ubfx` (unsigned bit field extract) instructions to pull out specific bit ranges from the underlying 64-bit storage. The key is understanding how these bitfield definitions are actually constructed and whether they're properly aligned with the instruction encoding.\\n\\nLet me try a different debugging approach—I'll add a print statement directly into the generated decode-method code right after the initial switch statement to see what's actually being executed.\",\"signature\":\"be6efcd579fc048a7bb201836f5cb6aafb23749c615f5996c1e1be6d79b0ba4b\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":125,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":139859},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"f495eac3-1617-4374-a892-a7510248c135\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:08:32.589Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"