essage\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"The decode-method.cc.inc and decoder.o are from 13:08, but gem5.opt is from 13:13. The gem5.opt was rebuilt AFTER the decoder.o. But the decode-method.cc.inc was NOT recompiled (it's older). The gem5.opt must be using a cached or old decoder.o.\\n\\nActually wait - let me think about this differently. The gem5.opt was linked at 13:13. The decoder.o is from 13:08. If the linker used a stale decoder.o, that would explain why \\\"DBG decodeInst\\\" isn't in gem5.opt.\\n\\nBut why would the linker use a stale object file? Let me check if maybe the SCons build system detected that gem5.opt was \\\"up to date\\\" with respect to decoder.o (because decoder.o wasn't changed between builds). Actually no - gem5.opt is newer (13:13) than decoder.o (13:08). So gem5.opt should include the latest decoder.o.\\n \\nThe fact that `DBG UndefinedInstruction::invoke` IS showing up in the binary but `DBG decodeInst` isn't means the linker definitely rebuilt gem5.opt, yet somehow the decoder.o content wasn't included. This is really strange - either there's another decoder object file being used, or the build system is doing something unexpected with the linking process.\\n\\nLet me search the entire binary for \\\"DBG decodeInst\\\" to see if it's actually compiled in somewhere else, and also check the decode-method.cc.inc file to verify it still has the debug output.\",\"signature\":\"b095b82987e69f7eb724dc84a93c84a228a577ec30530caa8ff4e2253f404acf\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":218,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":124,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":145532},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"b10968d8-bea7-4af0-900c-1f830497dee3\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:14:39.688Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionI