64` constructor to see what's actually being returned.\\n\\nI should verify whether my earlier debug statements are even in the current binary or if it's still stale.\",\"signature\":\"836ed6320f7f209b37279a32d21071053917872841c6d3b52ab3edf1ddd9f128\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":165868},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"b5a4fea6-ae16-492f-9f17-5f5dc396737e\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:27:10.960Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"b5a4fea6-ae16-492f-9f17-5f5dc396737e\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d312483ec894922cc86e5469ee9b7\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_function_u8to1fd9dxrb_1\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"strings /Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5/build/ARM/gem5.opt 2>/dev/null | grep \\\"DBG\\\"\"}}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":165868,\"output_tokens\":332,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"5755a7ef-8596-431a-b40b-fcd94d52328d\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:27:11.406Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"5755a7ef-8596-431a-b40b-fcd94d52328d\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"520da623-e17e-4efe-b292-47222de157e3\",\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_function_u8to1fd9dxrb_1\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"DBG UndefinedInstruction::invoke: unknown=%d enc=0x%08llx\\nDBG decodeInst ENTRY: mach=0x%llx\\nDBG bit27:25=111 case: mach=0x%llx\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"uuid\":\"0de60260-7b2f-47ab-8c6f-ce7a9ca17cba\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:27:11.570Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"5755a7ef-8596-431a-b40b-fcd94d52328d\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"0de60260-7b2f-47ab-8c6f-ce7a9ca17cba\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d312f0a6799915da0a7d247314044\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"All 3 debug strings are in the binary. But only 2 print. The third (bit27:25=111) doesn't print. This means the execution never reaches that code path.\\n\\nGiven the call flow:\\n1. `DBG decodeInst ENTRY: mach=0x1e2e1000` prints → `decodeInst` IS called with 0x1e2e1000\\n2. `DBG bit27:25=111 case` does NOT print → execution never reaches the else branch with bits27:25=111\\n3. `DBG UndefinedInstruction::invoke` prints → `Unknown64::execute` IS called\\n\\n\\nThe switch must be routing through a case 0x1 path instead. I should add debug to each switch case to trace exactly which path is being taken. Looking more carefully at the `decode-method.cc.inc` output, I'm examining the switch structure that starts at DEBUGSTEP and branches through ILLEGALEXEC, DECODERFAULT, and THUMB.\\n\\nAt THUMB=0, the code checks AARCH64 and finds case 0x1, which hits the AArch64 decoder. From there it evaluates the condition at bit 27: if that's 0, it checks bit 28 (SVE), and if bit 28 is 0, it continues checking additional conditions. But wait—the real puzzle is that my debug output in `decodeFpAdvSIMD` isn't firing at all, which suggests the code path I'm tracing might not be where the actual execution is happening. I'm seeing the bit-field access pattern used throughout the code for extracting instruction fields, so `bits(machInst, 27)` should work fine. But I should verify that `decodeFpAdvSIMD` in the source file is actually in the binary—let me search for its definition.\\n\\nThe function is declared as a template in the header and implemented in the decoder section, but it's not a template itself. It's defined in the decoder output block and included in the namespace where it's called, so it should be accessible.\\n\\nActually, I just realized something critical: `decodeFpMulMadd` is in a separate decoder output block in neon64.isa, which means it gets compiled into the `Aarch64` namespace within the `ArmISAInst` namespace. So when the code tries to call it from within the `Aarch64` namespace using `namespace Aarch64`, there shouldn't be a namespace mismatch.\\n\\nBut wait—let me check if there's actually a compilation error I'm missing, or if the function is being compiled into a different object file than expected.\\n\\nActually, the simplest approach is to just add a print statement directly at the call site to see if it ever gets hit. If the print doesn't show up when I run it, then I know the call site is never reached, which means the condition checking the AARCH64 bit must be failing.\\n\\nLet me try a different angle though—what if `bits()` on an ExtMachInst is actually extracting bits from the wrong location because of how the BitUnion is structured? Maybe the BitUnion64 is interpreting the 32-bit instruction encoding differently than I expect, so instead of checking the raw bits, I should decode the instruction first to understand what the bits actually represent.\\n\\nOr better yet, let me just add debug output at every single conditional branch and return statement in the decode-method section to see exactly which path gets taken.\",\"signature\":\"b50c147a505a35658658428c80f81d36de35d663d3ee58921735b37618d09b5c\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":166038},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"9b87311c-2ec1-4b1f-9118-2f611a209a9f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:27:35.675Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"9b87311c-2ec1-4b1f-9118-2f611a209a9f\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d312f0a6799915da0a7d247314044\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The function exists but isn't reached. Let me add debug at ALL branches to trace the exact path. First, let me add debug at the `case 0x1:` (AARCH64=1):\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":166038},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"aa00dc18-3427-46f3-b160-2f1d54ffaaf2\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:27:36.904Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"aa00dc18-3427-46f3-b160-2f1d54ffaaf2\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d312f0a6799915da0a7d247314044\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_function_u5dwwobv46fz_1\",\"name\":\"Edit\",\"input\":{\"replace_all\":false,\"file_path\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5/build/ARM/arch/arm/generated/decode-method.cc.inc\",\"old_string\":\"                    case 0x1:   \\n                      // Aarch64::aarch64(([], {}))\\n                      \\n                          {\\n                              using namespace Aarch64;\",\"new_string\":\"                    case 0x1:\\n                      // Aarch64::aarch64(([], {}))\\n                      fprintf(stderr, \\\"DBG AARCH64=1: mach=0x%llx\\\\n\\\", (unsigned long long)machInst); fflush(stderr);\\n                          {\\n                              using namespace Aarch64;\\n                              fprintf(stderr, \\\"DBG after using Aarch64: mach=0x%llx\\\\n\\\", (unsigned long long)machInst); fflush(stderr);\"}}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":166038,\"output_tokens\":953,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"4eb113ab-b77c-417a-95aa-bb91d79c43ec\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:27:40.797Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"4eb113ab-b77c-417a-95aa-bb91d79c43ec\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"520da623-e17e-4efe-b292-47222de157e3\",\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_function_u5dwwobv46fz_1\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"The file /Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5/build/ARM/arch/arm/generated/decode-method.cc.inc has been updated successfully.\"}]},\"uuid\":\"f4957183-1559-4cb0-82b2-ebf5eaf15e48\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:27:40.917Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"4eb113ab-b77c-417a-95aa-bb91d79c43ec\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":null,\"logicalParentUuid\":\"7d2b00bd-36c5-4886-bbdf-49b54a0c6ed0\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"compact_boundary\",\"content\":\"Conversation compacted\",\"isMeta\":false,\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:58:40.584Z\",\"uuid\":\"bfbc8588-f7b4-426b-a8c2-bbc86617ee99\",\"level\":\"info\",\"compactMetadata\":{\"trigger\":\"auto\",\"preTokens\":167089},\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"bfbc8588-f7b4-426b-a8c2-bbc86617ee99\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"520da623-e17e-4efe-b292-47222de157e3\",\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\\n\\nSummary:\\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\\n   The user asked to fix gem5 ARM64 SE mode decoder issues where instructions like FMADD, FMLA, FMLS, FMOV return \\\"GEM5_UNKNOWN_INST\\\" errors. The verification command is:\\n   ```\\n   ./build/ARM/gem5.opt configs/example/arm/sdc_baremetal_se.py /Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/test_neon.elf --max-ticks=1000000\\n   ```\\n   The crashing instruction is `inst 0x1e2e1000` (FMLS Sd,Sn,Sm).\\n\\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\\n   - gem5 ARM64 ISA decoder using `bitPatternMatcher` template-based pattern matching\\n   - ARM64 instruction encoding: bits are numbered 31 down to 0 in MSB-first order\\n   - FMLS instruction encoding: `0x1e2e1000` = `bits27:25=111`, `bits31:28=0x1`, `bit22=0`, `bit21=1`, `bit20=0`\\n   - `switchVal = (bits15:12 << 0) | (bits23:22 << 4)` = 0x02 for FMLS (matches FADD case)\\n   - `isFpDataProc2Source` pattern: `bit21=X, bit20=X, bit15:12=XXXX, bit23:22=XX` (bit21 is wildcard)\\n   - The FMLS path: top-level → `bits27:25=111` → `decodeFpAdvSIMD<GenericDecoder>` → `isConvFloatPFixedP` (bit22=1? No, FMLS bit22=0) → `isFpMulMadd` (NEW) → `decodeFpMulMadd`\\n   - Pattern group mapping in `bitPatternMatcher<31,10,...>`: groups map to bits 31:28, 27:25, 24:23, 22:19, 18:15, 14:10 (22 bits total)\\n   - `bits(machInst, msb, lsb)` returns `(val >> lsb) & ((1 << nbits) - 1)`\\n   - `isUnknown()` returns true when `StaticInst::isUnknown()` is true\\n\\n3. Files and Code Sections:\\n\\n   - `/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5/src/arch/arm/isa/formats/aarch64.isa`\\n     - **Primary decoder file** - all pattern definitions and decode function declarations live here\\n     - `isFpMulMadd` pattern (NEW - added):\\n       ```python\\n       inline constexpr auto isFpMulMadd = bitPatternMatcher<\\n           MachInst,\\n           31, 10,\\n           '0','0','0','1', // op0: bits31:28=0001\\n           '1','1','1',\\n           '0','0',         // op1: bits27:24=0110 (bit24=0 already enforced)\\n           '0','X','X','X', // op2: bit23=0, bits22:20=XXX\\n           'X','X','X','X', // op3: bits19:16=XXXX\\n           'X','X','X','X','X'>(); // op3: bits15:10=XXXXX\\n       ```\\n     - `isConvFloatPFixedP` pattern (MODIFIED - added `bit22=1`):\\n       ```python\\n       inline constexpr auto isConvFloatPFixedP = bitPatternMatcher<\\n           MachInst,\\n           31, 10,\\n           'X','0','X','1', // op0\\n           '1','1','1',\\n           '0','0', // op1: bits27:26=00 (bit25=0), bit24:23=00 (bit24=0, bit23=0)\\n           '1','X','X','X', // op2: bit22=1, bits21:19=XXX\\n           'X','X','X','X','X','X','X','X','X'>(); // op3\\n       ```\\n     - `isFpDataProc1Source` pattern (MODIFIED - added `bit22=1`):\\n       ```python\\n       inline constexpr auto isFpDataProc1Source = bitPatternMatcher<\\n           MachInst,\\n           31, 10,\\n           'X','0','X','1', // op0\\n           '1','1','1',\\n           '0','X', // op1\\n           '1','X','X','X', // op2: bit22=1 (excludes FMLA/FMLS which have bit22=0)\\n           'X','X','X','X','1','0','0','0','0'>(); // op3\\n       ```\\n     - `decodeFpAdvSIMD` routing (MODIFIED - `isFpMulMadd` moved before `isFpDataProc1Source`):\\n       ```\\n       if (isConvFloatPFixedP(machInst)) return decodeFpConvFixed(machInst);\\n       if (isConvFloatPInt(machInst)) return decodeFpConvFp(machInst);\\n       if (isFpMulMadd(machInst)) return decodeFpMulMadd(machInst);\\n       if (isFpDataProc1Source(machInst)) return decodeFpDataProc1Source(machInst);\\n       if (isFpCompare(machInst)) return decodeFpCompare(machInst);\\n       if (isFpImmediate(machInst)) return decodeFpImmediate(machInst);\\n       if (isFpCondCompare(machInst)) return decodeFpCondCompare(machInst);\\n       if (isFpDataProc2Source(machInst)) return decodeFpDataProc2Source(machInst);\\n       ```\\n\\n   - `/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5/src/arch/arm/isa/formats/neon64.isa`\\n     - Added declaration for `decodeFpMulMadd`:\\n       ```python\\n       // FMLA/FMLS: scalar three-same FP (bit21=1, bit15=1)\\n       inline StaticInstPtr decodeFpMulMadd(ExtMachInst machInst);\\n       ```\\n     - Added implementation:\\n       ```python\\n       StaticInstPtr\\n       decodeFpMulMadd(ExtMachInst machInst)\\n       {\\n           uint8_t q      = bits(machInst, 30);\\n           uint8_t size   = bits(machInst, 23, 22);\\n           uint8_t opcode = bits(machInst, 14, 10);  // 5-bit opcode\\n\\n           RegIndex vd = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 4, 0);\\n           RegIndex vn = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 9, 5);\\n           RegIndex vm = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 20, 16);\\n\\n           switch (size) {\\n             case 0: // 16-bit (half-precision)\\n               if (opcode & 1) { // FMLA\\n                   if (q) return new FmlaQX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n                   else return new FmlaDX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n               } else { // FMLS\\n                   if (q) return new FmlsQX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n                   else return new FmlsDX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n               }\\n             case 1: // 32-bit (single-precision)\\n               if (opcode & 1) { // FMLA\\n                   if (q) return new FmlaQX<uint32_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n                   else return new FmlaDX<uint32_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n               }\\n               return new Unknown64(machInst);\\n             default:\\n               return new Unknown64(machInst);\\n           }\\n       }\\n       ```\\n\\n   - `/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5/src/base/bitfield.hh`\\n     - Contains `bitPatternMatcher` implementation:\\n       ```cpp\\n       template<typename T, int msb, int lsb, char curr, char... rest>\\n       constexpr auto bitPatternMatcher() {\\n           static_assert(msb >= 0 && lsb >= 0 && msb - lsb == sizeof...(rest));\\n           constexpr T mask = dontCareMask<T, msb, lsb, curr, rest...>();\\n           constexpr T match = bitMatch<T, msb, lsb, curr, rest...>();\\n           auto ret = [] (T value) constexpr {\\n               return (value & mask) == match;\\n           };\\n           return ret;\\n       }\\n       ```\\n\\n4. Errors and fixes:\\n   - **Wrong function for guard**: Added FMLA/FMLS guard `bit21=1 && opcode>=0x19` in `decodeFpDataProc1Source` — but FMLS routes to `decodeFpDataProc2Source` not `decodeFpDataProc1Source`. Fixed by removing the guard.\\n   - **Wrong bit15 value**: Initially set `bit15=1` in `isFpMulMadd` pattern. ARM encoding has `bit15=0` for FMLS/FMLA. Fixed pattern to use `X` for bit15.\\n   - **6-bit vs 5-bit opcode**: Used `bits(machInst, 15, 10)` (6-bit) but should use `bits(machInst, 14, 10)` (5-bit). FMLS 5-bit opcode = 0x04, FMLA = 0x0B.\\n   - **Pattern size mismatch**: 20 chars provided but 22 needed (bits 31-10). Fixed by adding missing char groups.\\n   - **Guard ordering**: Guard in `decodeFpDataProc2Source` fired BEFORE `isFpMulMadd` was checked in the if-chain, returning Unknown64 before `isFpMulMadd` was ever reached. Fixed by removing the guard.\\n   - **Stale build**: Several incremental builds may have cached old binary. Clean rebuild performed.\\n   - **Header corruption from clean**: Running `scons --clean` broke generated headers (`enums/TypeTLB.hh` missing). Fixed by running `scons` again which regenerated all targets.\\n\\n5. Problem Solving:\\n   - **SOLVED**: Identified root cause — FMLS `switchVal=0x02` matches FADD in `decodeFpDataProc2Source`\\n   - **SOLVED**: Identified that FMLS should be caught by NEON scalar 3-same path but scalar FP checks intercept it first\\n   - **SOLVED**: Python simulation confirms `isFpMulMadd` pattern matches `0x1e2e1000` correctly\\n   - **ONGOING**: Despite pattern matching being correct and binary containing both `decodeFpAdvSIMD<GenericDecoder>` and `decodeFpMulMadd`, the instruction still returns Unknown64 at runtime\\n   - **Key insight discovered**: `isUnknown()` path means the instruction class's `StaticInst::isUnknown()` returns true. Even `FmlsDX<uint16_t>` constructor exists in the binary (`nm` shows `FmlsDXIjE` symbols). The decode is being called but returning something marked as unknown.\\n   - **Critical discovery**: After the last clean rebuild, the instruction STILL fails with \\\"unknown\\\" (not \\\"unimplemented\\\"), meaning the StaticInst is being created but marked as unknown.\\n\\n6. All user messages:\\n   - \\\"FIX GEM5 DECODER: 修复 gem5 ARM64 指令解码器问题\\\" — Detailed problem description requesting fix for FMADD/FMLA/FMOV instructions failing to decode, with root cause analysis pointing to `isFpDataProc1Source` pattern and FMADD/FMLA routing issues\\n   - Multiple tool results showing continued failures (exit code 134, panic with unknown instruction)\\n\\n7. Pending Tasks:\\n   - Get `test_neon.elf` to run successfully in gem5 without unknown instruction errors\\n   - Verify the fix works end-to-end\\n   - Potentially test other ELFs from the artifacts directory\\n\\n8. Current Work:\\n   Immediately before this summary, I had just discovered that `decodeFpAdvSIMD<GenericDecoder>` and `decodeFpMulMadd` both exist as symbols in the compiled binary, yet the instruction `0x1e2e1000` still returns \\\"unknown\\\" (not \\\"unimplemented\\\"). The decode chain is:\\n   ```\\n   decodeAarch64Inst(machInst=0x1e2e1000)\\n     → bits27:25=111 → decodeFpAdvSIMD<GenericDecoder>(machInst)\\n       → isConvFloatPFixedP? bit22=1 needed → 0x1e2e1000 bit22=0 → FALSE\\n       → isFpMulMadd? → pattern should match (verified in Python)\\n         → decodeFpMulMadd(machInst)\\n           → size=bits23:22=0 → case 0\\n           → opcode=bits14:10=0x04\\n           → opcode & 1 = 0 → FMLS\\n           → q=bits30=0 → return new FmlsDX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm)\\n   ```\\n   The `nm` command confirmed both functions exist:\\n   - `REDACTED...EE` (text, defined)\\n   - `REDACTED...EE` (text, defined)\\n   \\n   The mystery is why the decode returns Unknown64 despite the routing appearing correct.\\n\\n9. Optional Next Step:\\n   The next step is to investigate WHY `decodeFpMulMadd` returns an instruction marked as unknown. Possible causes to investigate:\\n   - Whether `FmlsDX`/`FmlaDX`/`FmlsQX`/`FmlaQX` template instantiations are actually compiled into the binary (`nm` showed they exist for `<uint16_t>` and `<uint32_t>`)\\n   - Whether the AtomicSimpleCPU is actually calling `decodeFpAdvSIMD<GenericDecoder>` vs some other decoder template\\n   - Whether the NEON64 decoder in neon64.isa is being compiled into the ARM build (the file `neon64.isa` is processed by gem5's ISA compiler, but the binary needs to be verified)\\n   - Whether there's a different instruction class for the FMLS scalar variant that must be used instead of the NEON vector variant\\n\\n   Relevant quote from the last working section: \\\"Both functions exist in the binary. Let me check the routing order in the generated decoder\\\" — the investigation was tracing through the actual decode path to find where it diverges from the expected path.\\n\\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/wangxu/.claude/projects/-Users-wangxu-1-project-sdc-fuzzing/d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1.jsonl\\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \\\"I'll continue\\\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\"},\"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly\":true,\"isCompactSummary\":true,\"uuid\":\"ddb7705f-6ae4-4582-85ea-7f714949cfc7\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:58:40.585Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"ddb7705f-6ae4-4582-85ea-7f714949cfc7\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d1c70eca5c245fc643d90df3e3784\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Let me investigate why `decodeFpMulMadd` returns an instruction marked as unknown. The key issue is that even though the decode function exists and is being called, the returned instruction is marked as unknown. Let me check:\\n\\n1. Whether the instruction constructors are actually compiled in\\n2. Whether there's a routing issue at the top level\\n3. Whether the `AtomicSimpleCPU` uses a different decoder path\\n\\nLet me check the generated decoder files and the routing more carefully.\",\"signature\":\"3a3877c88f879beb3274e052d4ec27fa4930cfc1aea95400ab32c92288cc9937\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":9051,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":25545},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"a1e663d5-397a-44f2-a065-04d0f840ef9c\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:58:45.894Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"a1e663d5-397a-44f2-a065-04d0f840ef9c\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d1c70eca5c245fc643d90df3e3784\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me check the generated decoder to understand the exact routing at the top level.\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":9051,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":25545},\"service_