EN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.\\n37\\t\\n38\\tlet {{\\n39\\t    vfpEnabledCheckCode = '''\\n40\\t    {\\n41\\t        Fault fault = checkAdvSIMDOrFPEnabled32(xc->tcBase(),\\n42\\t                                                Cpsr, Cpacr, Nsacr, Fpexc,\\n43\\t                                                true, false);\\n44\\t        if (fault != NoFault)\\n45\\t            return fault;\\n46\\t    }\\n47\\t    '''\\n48\\t\\n49\\t    vfp64EnabledCheckCode = '''\\n50\\t    {\\n51\\t        Fault fault = checkFPAdvSIMDEnabled64(xc->tcBase(), Cpsr, Cpacr64);\\n52\\t        if (fault != NoFault)\\n53\\t             return fault;\\n54\\t    }\\n55\\t    '''\\n56\\t\\n57\\t    vmsrEnabledCheckCode = '''\\n58\\t    {\\n59\\t        Fault fault = NoFault;\\n60\\t        if (dest == (int)MISCREG_FPSCR) {\\n61\\t            fault = checkAdvSIMDOrFPEnabled32(xc->tcBase(),\\n62\\t                                              Cpsr, Cpacr, Nsacr, Fpexc,\\n63\\t                                              true, false);\\n64\\t        } else if (!inPrivilegedMode(Cpsr)) {\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"uuid\":\"b0f760f0-bc34-401a-840b-363a1d3c5cbd\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:01:17.953Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"63bb3542-33b9-4bbc-b222-287aa51cf3bd\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"b0f760f0-bc34-401a-840b-363a1d3c5cbd\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d1d0e9db365b5250cf59f71ba14b6\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"So `simd64EnabledCheckCode` (which is `vfp64EnabledCheckCode`) checks `checkFPAdvSIMDEnabled64`. This checks the CPACR (or CPACR64 for ARM64) to see if FP/SIMD is enabled. If it's disabled, it returns a `UndefinedInstruction` fault.\\n\\nThis means the issue is not with the decoder at all - it's with the **CPU configuration**. The CPU needs to have FP/SIMD enabled in the system. In the SE mode config, the AtomicSimpleCPU might not have FP/SIMD enabled.\\n\\nLet me check the system configuration. The issue might be in how the bare-metal config sets up the CPU. The system uses `ArmCpuCluster` and `SimpleSeSystem`. \\n\\nI need to trace through the configuration setup to see if the FP and SIMD extensions are being properly initialized in the system parameters.\",\"signature\":\"6cff27640407143cdb799dc794f9378b54eae8a7b3fd56709c152c64d122bdbd\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":624,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":52177},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"85176b99-23a0-4684-8c25-6d7297fd3ea9\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:01:23.186Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"85176b99-23a0-4684-8c25-6d7297fd3ea9\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d1d0e9db365b5250cf59f71ba14b6\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The check is `checkFPAdvSIMDEnabled64` - this verifies CPACR/CPACR64. The issue is likely the **CPU config doesn't have FP/SIMD enabled**. Let me check:\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax