\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"81450\\t    decodeFpDataProc2Source(ExtMachInst machInst)\\n81451\\t    {\\n81452\\t        if (bits(machInst, 31) ||\\n81453\\t                bits(machInst, 29)) {\\n81454\\t            return new Unknown64(machInst);\\n81455\\t        }\\n81456\\t        RegIndex rd = (RegIndex)(uint32_t)bits(machInst,  4,  0);\\n81457\\t        RegIndex rn = (RegIndex)(uint32_t)bits(machInst,  9,  5);\\n81458\\t        RegIndex rm = (RegIndex)(uint32_t)bits(machInst, 20, 16);\\n81459\\t        uint8_t switchVal = (bits(machInst, 15, 12) << 0) |\\n81460\\t                            (bits(machInst, 23, 22) << 4);\\n81461\\t        switch (switchVal) {\\n81462\\t          case 0x00: // FMUL Sd = Sn * Sm\\n81463\\t            return new FMulS(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81464\\t          case 0x10: // FMUL Dd = Dn * Dm\\n81465\\t            return new FMulD(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81466\\t          case 0x30: // FMUL Hd = Hn * Hm\\n81467\\t            return new FMulH(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81468\\t          case 0x01: // FDIV Sd = Sn / Sm\\n81469\\t            return new FDivS(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81470\\t          case 0x11: // FDIV Dd = Dn / Dm\\n81471\\t            return new FDivD(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81472\\t          case 0x31: // FDIV Hd = Hn / Hm\\n81473\\t            return new FDivH(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81474\\t          case 0x02: // FADD Sd = Sn + Sm\\n81475\\t            return new FAddS(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81476\\t          case 0x12: // FADD Dd = Dn + Dm\\n81477\\t            return new FAddD(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81478\\t          case 0x32: // FADD Hd = Hn + Hm\\n81479\\t            return new FAddH(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81480\\t          case 0x03: // FSUB Sd = Sn - Sm\\n81481\\t            return new FSubS(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81482\\t          case 0x13: // FSUB Dd = Dn - Dm\\n81483\\t            return new FSubD(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81484\\t          case 0x33: // FSUB Hd = Hn - Hm\\n81485\\t            return new FSubH(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81486\\t          case 0x04: // FMAX Sd = max(Sn, Sm)\\n81487\\t            return new FMaxS(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81488\\t          case 0x14: // FMAX Dd = max(Dn, Dm)\\n81489\\t            return new FMaxD(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81490\\t          case 0x34: // FMAX Hd = max(Hn, Hm)\\n81491\\t            return new FMaxH(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81492\\t          case 0x05: // FMIN Sd = min(Sn, Sm)\\n81493\\t            return new FMinS(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81494\\t          case 0x15: // FMIN Dd = min(Dn, Dm)\\n81495\\t            return new FMinD(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81496\\t          case 0x35: // FMIN Hd = min(Hn, Hm)\\n81497\\t            return new FMinH(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81498\\t          case 0x06: // FMAXNM Sd = maxNum(Sn, Sm)\\n81499\\t            return new FMaxNMS(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81500\\t          case 0x16: // FMAXNM Dd = maxNum(Dn, Dm)\\n81501\\t            return new FMaxNMD(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81502\\t          case 0x36: // FMAXNM Hd = maxNum(Hn, Hm)\\n81503\\t            return new FMaxNMH(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81504\\t          case 0x07: // FMINNM Sd = minNum(Sn, Sm)\\n81505\\t            return new FMinNMS(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81506\\t          case 0x17: // FMINNM Dd = minNum(Dn, Dm)\\n81507\\t            return new FMinNMD(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n81508\\t          case 0x37: // FMINNM Hd = minNum(Hn, Hm)\\n81509\\t            return new FMinNMH(machInst, rd, rn, rm);\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"uuid\":\"d52b7809-604e-4f0a-988b-c2c368623f21\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:30:16.573Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"a2cdfa21-7d0a-418