me search through the `decode-method.cc.inc` file to see if there's a duplicate definition of `isFpMulMadd` that might be shadowing the correct one.\\n\\nActually, I'm noticing the `using namespace ArmISAInst;` directive in the decode method—that's just opening up the class names without affecting any namespace-scoped functions. The `Aarch64` namespace functions should be called directly. But now I'm looking at `decodeFpMulMadd` more closely, particularly the opcode extraction logic...\\n\\nWait, I'm seeing the real issue now. The generated code for `decodeFpMulMadd` has `case 0:` that falls through without a return statement, so execution continues into the next case block. That's causing the wrong instruction to be returned. Tracing through the FMLS case with `0x1e2e1000`: the size extracts to 0 (half-precision), the opcode is 0x04, and `opcode & 1` evaluates to 0, so it should return a 16-bit FmlsDX instruction—but the missing return is letting it fall through to case 1.\\n\\nI need to add the break statements to properly exit each case, then rebuild and test to see if the panic clears up. Actually, wait—the panic happens during decoding, not execution, so this fallthrough might not be the root cause. Let me verify the binary is actually using the new generated code and check if there's a stale object file with old code that's being linked instead.\",\"signature\":\"929832eee0c1a57f75bda2e4e11c38af1b428b9698426b5b11f4d445e734d9e6\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":109414},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"b724cf26-7a1e-4689-bf13-b3c7d6c5134a\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:30:55.364Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\