5:46:01.839Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"3500291b-e115-46a7-80fb-7571f6bf3abe\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"520da623-e17e-4efe-b292-47222de157e3\",\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_function_eksou9hl0pjm_1\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"40\\t\\n41\\tBareMetalWorkload::BareMetalWorkload(const Params &p) : SEWorkload(p)\\n42\\t{}\\n43\\t\\n44\\tvoid\\n45\\tBareMetalWorkload::initState()\\n46\\t{\\n47\\t    SEWorkload::initState();\\n48\\t\\n49\\t    // Get entry point from the first process via ThreadContext\\n50\\t    ThreadContext *tc = system->threads[0];\\n51\\t    Process *proc = tc->getProcessPtr();\\n52\\t\\n53\\t    // CRITICAL: Call the Process subclass's initState() explicitly\\n54\\t    // This ensures ArmBareMetalProcess64::initState() is called which maps pages\\n55\\t    proc->initState();\\n56\\t\\n57\\t    // Get entry after process initState (in case it changes)\\n58\\t    Addr entry = proc->objFile->entryPoint();\\n59\\t\\n60\\t    // Set PC via ArmPCState\\n61\\t    ArmISA::PCState pc;\\n62\\t    pc.pc(entry);\\n63\\t    tc->pcState(pc);\\n64\\t\\n65\\t    // Activate first thread, suspend others\\n66\\t    for (auto *tc: system->threads) {\\n67\\t        if (tc->contextId() == 0) {\\n68\\t            tc->activate();\\n69\\t        } else {\\n70\\t            tc->suspend();\\n71\\t        }\\n72\\t    }\\n73\\t}\\n74\\t\\n75\\t} // namespace ArmISA\\n76\\t\\n77\\tnamespace\\n78\\t{\\n79\\t\\n80\\t/**\\n81\\t * BareMetalLoader — matches ARM64/ARM bare-metal ELFs (no OSABI = SYSV or ELF\\n82\\t * with OSABI set to something other than Linux/FreeBSD) and instantiates\\n83\\t * ArmBareMetalProcess instead of ArmProcess64/ArmLinuxProcess64.\\n84\\t *\\n85\\t * The loader is registered via static initialization so it participates in\\n86\\t * Process::tryLoaders().  It only matches when:\\n87\\t *   - Architecture is Arm64, Arm, or Thumb\\n88\\t *   - Operating system is Unknown (not Linux / FreeBSD / etc.)\\n89\\t *   - No ELF interpreter is present (static binaries only)\\n90\\t */\\n91\\tclass BareMetalLoader : public Process::Loader\\n92\\t{\\n93\\t  public:\\n94\\t    Process *\\n95\\t    load(const ProcessParams &params, loader::ObjectFile *obj) override\\n96\\t    {\\n97\\t        auto arch = obj->getArch();\\n98\\t        auto opsys = obj->getOpSys();\\n99\\t\\n100\\t        // Only handle ARM architectures\\n101\\t        if (arch != loader::Arm && arch != loader::Thumb &&\\n102\\t            arch != loader::Arm64) {\\n103\\t            return nullptr;\\n104\\t        }\\n105\\t\\n106\\t        // Only handle truly bare-metal binaries (no OS, or explicit bare-metal)\\n107\\t        // If it's Linux, FreeBSD, or other OS — let the appropriate loader handle it\\n108\\t        if (opsys != loader::UnknownOpSys)\\n109\\t            return nullptr;\\n110\\t\\n111\\t        // Bare-metal ELF should have no interpreter (static binary)\\n112\\t        if (obj->getInterpreter())\\n113\\t            return nullptr;\\n114\\t\\n115\\t        // Create the appropriate ArmBareMetalProcess based on word width\\n116\\t        if (arch == loader::Arm64)\\n117\\t            return new ArmISA::ArmBareMetalProcess64(params, obj, arch);\\n118\\t        else\\n119\\t            return new ArmISA::ArmBareMetalProcess32(params, obj, arch);\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"uuid\