ant\",\"uuid\":\"eeb465ac-4259-4052-9029-88f5ff48dd0f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:47:28.607Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"eeb465ac-4259-4052-9029-88f5ff48dd0f\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"520da623-e17e-4efe-b292-47222de157e3\",\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_function_3aj6lelpbxwm_1\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/test_neon.elf: ELF 64-bit LSB executable, ARM aarch64, version 1 (SYSV), statically linked, not stripped\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"uuid\":\"4c797a53-79cc-43d6-b0d2-1ee07341a11d\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:47:28.753Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"eeb465ac-4259-4052-9029-88f5ff48dd0f\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"4c797a53-79cc-43d6-b0d2-1ee07341a11d\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d35f135559de088c24e5a3e6068f5\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Confirmed: the ELF is ARM aarch64 (64-bit). So the PC's AARCH64 bit should be set.\\n\\nLet me wait for the build and test. While waiting, let me think about other potential issues...\\n\\nActually, I realize I should also check what `emi.instBits` is for FMLS. In the `process()` method:```cpp\\nif (!emi.thumb) {    emi.instBits = data;\\n    if (!emi.aarch64) {        emi.sevenAndFour = bits(data, 7) && bits(data, 4);\\n        emi.isMisc = (bits(data, 24, 23) == 0x2 && bits(data, 20) == 0);\\n    }\\n    consumeBytes(4);\\n```\\n\\nSince `emi.thumb = false` and `emi.aarch64 = false` (both from PC), `emi.instBits` gets set to the 32-bit value `0x1e2e1000`, and `emi.sevenAndFour` is also computed. Since `emi.aarch64` is false, the AArch64 bitfield `Bitfield<34> aarch64` remains unset (0).\\n\\nNow I'm tracing through how the `switch (AARCH64)` statement evaluates—when the code references `AARCH64` in the switch, it's using a bitfield accessor on the ExtMachInst object, which returns the value at bit position 34. Since that bit is 0, the switch goes to the default case, which in the ARMv8 decode path handles non-AArch64 instructions.\\n\\nBut the mystery is that the debug output shows `DBG decodeInst ENTRY` firing with the correct instruction, yet there's no subsequent debug line for the `bit27:25=111` case that should trigger for this instruction.\\n\\nLet me reconsider the switch structure—maybe `bit27:25=111` isn't actually nested within the AARCH64 switch I think it is. The debug at line 2916 should fire if we reach that point, but we never see it, which means execution must be hitting a return statement somewhere earlier in the decode chain, likely in the AARCH64=0 path where FMLS would return as Unknown.\\n\\nI need to trace through the nested switch cases more carefully—after the COND_CODE switch closes around line 296, there's a default case that handles unknown conditions, and that path appears to lead to an ARM32 Neon decode routine based on the bit pattern matching.\\n\\nBut wait, let me reconsider the execution flow: if we're hitting `Unknown` repeatedly, maybe the real issue is that the AARCH64 bit should actually be set to 1 in the decoded instruction, which would route us to the AARCH64=1 case instead. Let me verify whether the AARCH64 field is properly configured in the ExtMachInst structure.\\n\\nActually, I'm noticing something in the PC state setup—in the bare-metal workload initialization, the PC is being set via `pc.pc(entry)` and then `tc->pcState(pc)`. I need to trace through how that gets converted and whether the AARCH64 flag is being preserved correctly through that chain.\",\"signature\":\"672737e8a853d35e07c9b73353debbff25ffd76679a8a33966ad3d19020b7b1c\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":218,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":268,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":80310},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"9bbfa06f-8ed0-4f6e-9c19-4205f727bb78\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:47:50.445Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"9bbfa06f-8ed0-4f6e-9c19-4205f727bb78\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d35f135559de088c24e5a3e6068f5\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The ELF is confirmed ARM aarch64. While building, let me trace how the PC state flows through to the decoder's AARCH64 bit.\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":218,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":268,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":80310},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"f53ab0b0-7bb4-485e-9646-cac650516b16\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:47:51.061Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"f53ab0b0-7bb4-485e-9646-cac650516b16\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d35f135559de088c24e5a3e6068f5\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"ass