\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"ba673a17-aa9f-4952-b871-70237dadcc47\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"f0504b47-17c9-4bb4-afb0-5fee28a51291\",\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_function_58j4vjldmyij_1\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"82203\\t    decodeFpMulMadd(ExtMachInst machInst)\\n82204\\t    {\\n82205\\t        // DEBUG: log when this function is called\\n82206\\t        fprintf(stderr, \\\"DEBUG decodeFpMulMadd called: machInst=0x%llx\\\\n\\\", (unsigned long long)machInst);\\n82207\\t        uint32_t inst32 = (uint32_t)(machInst & 0xFFFFFFFF);\\n82208\\t        fprintf(stderr, \\\"DEBUG: inst32=0x%08x, bits31:28=0x%x, bits27:24=0x%x, bits23:22=0x%x\\\\n\\\",\\n82209\\t                inst32, (inst32 >> 28) & 0xF, (inst32 >> 24) & 0xF, (inst32 >> 22) & 0x3);\\n82210\\t\\n82211\\t        uint8_t q      = bits(machInst, 30);\\n82212\\t        uint8_t size   = bits(machInst, 23, 22);\\n82213\\t        // 5-bit opcode: bits(14,10).  FMLS=0x04 (bit1=0), FMLA=0x0B (bit1=1).\\n82214\\t        uint8_t opcode = bits(machInst, 14, 10);\\n82215\\t\\n82216\\t        RegIndex vd = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 4, 0);\\n82217\\t        RegIndex vn = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 9, 5);\\n82218\\t        RegIndex vm = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 20, 16);\\n82219\\t\\n82220\\t        // opcode & 1: 0=FMLS, 1=FMLA\\n82221\\t        // For FMLS only 16-bit elements are valid; 32/64-bit return Unknown.\\n82222\\t        switch (size) {\\n82223\\t          case 0: // 16-bit elements (half-precision)\\n82224\\t            if (opcode & 1) { // FMLA\\n82225\\t                if (q)\\n82226\\t                    return new FmlaQX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n82227\\t                else\\n82228\\t                    return new FmlaDX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n82229\\t            } else { // FMLS\\n82230\\t                if (q)\\n82231\\t                    return new FmlsQX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n82232\\t                else\\n82233\\t                    return new FmlsDX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n82234\\t            }\\n82235\\t          case 1: // 32-bit elements (single-precision)\\n82236\\t            // FMLS is not defined for single-precision scalar; only FMLA.\\n82237\\t            if (opcode & 1) { // FMLA\\n82238\\t                if (q)\\n82239\\t                    return new FmlaQX<uint32_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n82240\\t                else\\n82241\\t                    return new FmlaDX<uint32_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n82242\\t            }\\n82243\\t            return new Unknown64(machInst);\\n82244\\t          default:\\n82245\\t            return new Unknown64(machInst);\\n82246\\t        }\\n82247\\t    }\\n82248\\t\\n82249\\t    StaticInstPtr\\n82250\\t    decodeNeon3SameFp16(ExtMachInst machInst)\\n82251\\t    {\\n82252\\t        uint8_t u_a_opcode = bits(machInst, 29) << 4 | // u\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"uuid\":\"c6e32867-4d84-48ac-8de0-fa94a1225e0f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:49:46.269Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"ba673a17-aa9f-4952-b871-70237dadcc47\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n","prompt":"请继续修复 gem5 decoder 问题。","result":"{\"parentUuid\":null,\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"520da623-e17e-4efe-b292-47222de157e3\",\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"FIX GEM5 DECODER: 修复 gem5 ARM64 指令解码器问题\\n\\n## 问题描述\\ngem5 SE 模式下，某些ARM64指令（如FMADD, FMLA, FMOV等）无法被正确解码，返回 \\\"GEM5_UNKNOWN_INST\\\" 错误。\\n\\n## 根因分析\\n在 `gem5/src/arch/arm/isa/formats/aarch64.isa` 中:\\n\\n1. **FMOV (0x1e204020)** 解码失败:\\n   - `isFpDataProc1Source` pattern 要求 bit[18]=1\\n   - 但 FMOV 的 bit[18]=0, 属于 \\\"FP Misc\\\" 指令\\n   \\n2. **FMADD/FMLA 等指令** 未被正确路由到 `decodeFpDataProc`\\n\\n## 修复任务\\n1. 分析 aarch64.isa 中的 pattern matcher 和 decode function 路由\\n2. 修复 isFpDataProc1Source 或添加新的 pattern 来匹配 FMOV\\n3. 确保 FMADD, FMLA 等指令能正确路由\\n4. 重新编译 gem5 (如果需要)\\n\\n## 关键文件\\n- gem5/src/arch/arm/isa/formats/aarch64.isa (decoder patterns)\\n- gem5/src/arch/arm/isa/formats/neon64.isa (NEON decode functions)\\n\\n## 验证\\n修复后运行测试:\\n```bash\\ncd /Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\\n./build/ARM/gem5.opt configs/example/arm/sdc_baremetal_se.py /Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/test_simple.elf\\n```\\n\\n需要看到正常退出而不是 \\\"unknown instruction\\\" 错误。\"},\"uuid\":\"f320cf06-6ac0-47b0-b553-388a72b6c345\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T02:25:42.707Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"c7b92c82-5641-46cf-96db-e688bc7d424a\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d06a77637952c9efe176644dfd184\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"The user wants me to fix gem5 ARM64 instruction decoder issues. Let me start by exploring the relevant files to understand the problem.\",\"signature\":\"0da406f9716cd7aa02a186ac4892aa1d5cabb9ec751d9083e93e49f23