 their values to verify the encoding matches what I'm seeing in the instruction encoding table.\\n\\nNow I'm checking the full 32-bit instruction against the expected pattern for the FMADD variant, working through each bit position systematically to confirm the opcode and operand fields align correctly.\\n\\nWait, I think I've been looking at the wrong bit pattern—I need to reconsider which instruction encoding I'm actually examining. Let me pull up the complete isFpDataProc pattern definition from the file to see the full context of what pattern I'm working with.\",\"signature\":\"8c1beeed0bb9d68754f09f4c21d941404dc469bad598c03891036dc98087fbdd\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1725,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":34678},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"8288f3ef-db7d-4140-92eb-f95850049d87\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T02:27:49.997Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"8288f3ef-db7d-4140-92eb-f95850049d87\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d06dc02f308a1a54696120c4401f5\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"\\nLet me read the key sections of the file more carefully.\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1725,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":34678},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"6cd5d46e-8280-4863-bd9d-3d60dd87aae2\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T02:27:50.507Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing