1` (32-bit single-precision). Let me check what happens in the existing NEON decoder for this:\\n```case 0b01001:  // FMLS    if (q)        return new FmlsQX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);    else        return new FmlsDX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);```It only handles `<uint16_t>`. What about 32-bit and 64-bit?\\n\\nFor `decodeNeon3SameFp16`:```case 0b00001:    if (q)        return new FmlaQX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);    else        return new FmlaDX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);```\\nAlso only `<uint16_t>`.\\n\\nSo for FMLA/FMLS with 32-bit elements, I only have `FmlaDX`/`FmlaQX`. The instruction sets `size=1` for 32-bit, but `decodeNeonSc3Same` checks `if (size == 1)` — let me verify this distinction. Looking at the scalar three same decoder, I see the size field is actually limited to specific values for FMLA and FMLS operations.\\n\\nFor the 16-bit case, FMLA dispatches through the floating-point decoder with `FmlaDX<FmlaQX>` for `<uint16_t>`, while FMLS follows a similar pattern but uses a different opcode value.\\n\\nWhen size equals 1 for 32-bit operations, the NEON scalar decoder routes both FMLA and FMLS to the same floating-point handler classes `FmlaDX`/`FmlaQX` for `<uint32_t>`. For 64-bit elements with size=2, there's no explicit handling, so these cases return Unknown.\\n\\nHowever, my current implementation always dispatches to Fmla regardless of whether it's actually FMLA or FMLS, since I haven't properly distinguished between the two instruction types yet. I need to use the opcode to determine which operation is being requested. I'm looking at how to distinguish FMLA from FMLS in the scalar FP instruction encoding—they both have the same opcode bits but differ in the opcode field itself (0x19 vs 0x1B). I can check `opcode & 0x2` to get the LSB of the 5-bit opcode field, which would be 0 for FMLA and 1 for FMLS, though I need to verify this is the right approach for the scalar FP encoding.\\n\\nActually, there's a cleaner pattern: checking `opcode & 1` gives me 1 for FMLA and 1 for FMLS, but checking `opcode & 2` gives me 0 for FMLA and 1 for FMLS—that's the actual distinguishing bit. So I can use that to branch between the two operations.\\n\\nNow I'm checking whether FMLS actually supports double-precision at all. Looking at the switch statement in the NEON scalar decoder, FMLS is only handled for `size == 0` (16-bit elements), and for `size == 1` (32-bit) or larger it returns an unknown instruction. This means FMLS might not be valid for double-precision, so I need to verify what the actual encoding constraints are before finalizing the instruction set.\\n\\nNow I'm ready to update the implementation to properly distinguish between FMLA and FMLS using the opcode LSB, with the size field determining the element width (0 for 16-bit, 1 for 32-bit, 2 for 64-bit), and returning an error for unsupported sizes.\\n\\nWriting the decode function... Writing the decoder logic...\",\"signature\":\"62e3236841f563f026440de3c3fc107559c5d1e13ccf1c332abba2243fbec309\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":154,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":96858},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"4fe6ea7f-b699-4866-a28e-35d864b53a41\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T02:53:18.721Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"4fe6ea7f-b699-4866-a28e-35d864b53a41\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d0d0623d296c2d5bd85321d45515e\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"`FmlsDX`/`FmlsQX` only exist for `<uint16_t>`. For 32-bit FMLS, gem5 returns `Unknown`. I'll update the implementation to properly distinguish FMLA vs FMLS using `opcode & 1` and handle sizes correctly.\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":154,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":96858},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"df88a95f-e62a-44af-97d0-34444772d951\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T02:53:20.599Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"df88a95f-e62a-44af-97d0-34444772d951\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d0d0623d296c2d5bd85321d45515e\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_function_vuosd83hcb37_1\",\"name\":\"Edit\",\"input\":{\"replace_all\":false,\"file_path\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5/src/arch/arm/isa/formats/neon64.isa\",\"old_string\":\"    // FMLA/FMLS: 31:24=00011110, 23:22=00, 21=1, 15=1, opcode in bits14:10\\n    // Encoding matches AdvSIMD scalar three-same; dispatch through\\n    // decodeNeonUThreeFpReg using the same (opcode, size, q) tuple.\\n    StaticInstPtr\\n    decodeFpMulMadd(ExtMachInst machInst)\\n    {\\n        uint8_t q     = bits(machInst, 30);\\n        uint8_t size  = bits(machInst, 23, 22);\\n\\n        RegIndex vd = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 4, 0);\\n        RegIndex vn = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 9, 5);\\n        RegIndex vm = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 20, 16);\\n\\n        // opcode: 0x19=FMLA, 0x1B=FMLS (bit14=1 for both, bits13:11 vary)\\n        // size selects element width: 0=16b, 1=32b, 2=64b\\n        switch (size) {\\n          case 0: // 16-bit elements (half-precision)\\n            if (q)\\n                return new FmlaQX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n            else\\n                return new FmlaDX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n          case 1: // 32-bit elements (single-precision)\\n            if (q)\\n                return new FmlaQX<uint32_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n            else\\n                return new FmlaDX<uint32_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n          case 2: // 64-bit elements (double-precision)\\n            if (q)\\n                return new FmlaQX<uint64_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n            else\\n                return new FmlaDX<uint64_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n          default:\\n            return new Unknown64(machInst);\\n        }\\n    }\",\"new_string\":\"    // FMLA/FMLS: 31:24=00011110, 23:22=00, 21=1, 15=1, opcode in bits14:10\\n    // Encoding matches AdvSIMD scalar three-same; dispatch through\\n    // decodeNeonUThreeFpReg using the same (opcode, size, q) tuple.\\n    StaticInstPtr\\n    decodeFpMulMadd(ExtMachInst machInst)\\n    {\\n        uint8_t q      = bits(machInst, 30);\\n        uint8_t size   = bits(machInst, 23, 22);\\n        uint8_t opcode = bits(machInst, 14, 10);\\n\\n        RegIndex vd = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 4, 0);\\n        RegIndex vn = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 9, 5);\\n        RegIndex vm = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 20, 16);\\n\\n        // opcode LSB distinguishes FMLA (0x19, bit0=1) from FMLS (0x1B, bit0=1):\\n        // FMLA: opcode & 1 = 1, FMLS: opcode & 1 = 1... wait:\\n        // 0x19 = 11001 -> bit0=1; 0x1B = 11011 -> bit0=1. Both have bit0=1!\\n        // So we check the raw opcode: 0x19=FMLA, 0x1B=FMLS.\\n        // For FMLS only 16-bit elements are valid; 32/64-bit return Unknown.\\n        switch (size) {\\n          case 0: // 16-bit elements (half-precision)\\n            if (opcode == 0x19) {\\n                if (q)\\n                    return new FmlaQX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n                else\\n                    return new FmlaDX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n            } else { // 0x1B = FMLS\\n                if (q)\\n                    return new FmlsQX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n                else\\n                    return new FmlsDX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n            }\\n          case 1: // 32-bit elements (single-precision)\\n            // FMLS is not defined for single-precision scalar; FMLA is.\\n            if (opcode == 0x19) {\\n                if (q)\\n                    return new FmlaQX<uint32_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n                else\\n                    return new FmlaDX<uint32_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n            }\\n            return new Unknown64(machInst);\\n          default:\\n            return new Unknown64(machInst);\\n        }\\n    }\"}}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":154,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":96858,\"output_tokens\":2086,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"9d65712a-6ec8-4b36-bede-566ed62c1fd8\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T02:53:40.432Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"9d65712a-6ec8-4b36-bede-566ed62c1fd8\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"520da623-e17e-4efe-b292-47222de157e3\",\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_function_vuosd83hcb37_1\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"The file /Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5/src/arch/a