e is triggering. Let me trace through what's actually happening with this instruction encoding. FMLS and FMLA don't actually conflict with the scalar FPADD instruction since they're assigned to different switch values, so I can remove the guard and add a dedicated pattern matcher instead.\",\"signature\":\"f65588dc0f630c2fab82a17caa48b099c020c7186f3f281c0bbecbb46eee535e\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":104793},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"369b2858-e09f-4086-9bc8-94fe419a6e5b\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:00:58.290Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"369b2858-e09f-4086-9bc8-94fe419a6e5b\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d0e9af9956f2bb3d96eb43c498bfb\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The guard is wrong - bit15=0 for FMLS/FMLA. The fix should be: no guard in `decodeFpDataProc2Source`, just add `isFpMulMadd` pattern BEFORE the scalar FP checks. Let me revert the guard and fix the routing.\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":104793},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"74df70d4-1341-44bc-b29d-f714f00f7c4c\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:01:00.543Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon