sn't matching any pattern at all, so I should verify the bit extraction logic is correct—checking whether the opcode is actually `0x04` after extracting bits 15-10 from the instruction. Now I'm mapping out the bit positions for the opcode extraction—bits 15 through 10 make up the 6-bit opcode field, so I need to shift right by 10 and mask with 0x3F to get the correct value. Let me trace through what the opcode actually is for this instruction and update the function accordingly.\",\"signature\":\"3cc25792ecdd2a5f1d9118cf5343b093f93871b00d839da406dcd5e98d77a6fb\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":105986},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"acd8d506-0409-4001-bf46-83931a6fa9c5\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:01:35.157Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"acd8d506-0409-4001-bf46-83931a6fa9c5\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d0f00ca25d8f07c63614e304d6d97\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The `decodeFpMulMadd` uses `bits(machInst, 14, 10)` which only gets 5 bits. I need to use `bits(machInst, 15, 10)` for the full 6-bit opcode.\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":105986},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"3a8975c8-3129-464b-bfbc-2bcc5815f6d5\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:01:36.588Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"3a8975c8-3129-464b-bfbc-2bcc5815f6d5\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d0f00ca25d8f07c63614e304d6d97\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_function_sb1hv8mkgx6x_1\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5/src/arch/arm/isa/formats/neon64.isa\",\"offset\":103,\"limit\":50}}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":105986,\"output_tokens\":549,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"efd6e9d9-4866-4661-91d5-f2cdc33726e1\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:01:37.205Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"efd6e9d9-4866-4661-91d5-f2cdc33726e1\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"520da623-e17e-4efe-b292-47222de157e3\",\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_function_sb1hv8mkgx6x_1\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"103\\toutput decoder {{\\n104\\tnamespace Aarch64\\n105\\t{\\n106\\t    // FMLA/FMLS: 31:24=00011110, 23:22=00, 21=1, 15=1, opcode in bits14:10\\n107\\t    // Encoding matches AdvSIMD scalar three-same; dispatch through\\n108\\t    // decodeNeonUThreeFpReg using the same (opcode, size, q) tuple.\\n109\\t    StaticInstPtr\\n110\\t    decodeFpMulMadd(ExtMachInst machInst)\\n111\\t    {\\n112\\t        uint8_t q      = bits(machInst, 30);\\n113\\t        uint8_t size   = bits(machInst, 23, 22);\\n114\\t        uint8_t opcode = bits(machInst, 14, 10);\\n115\\t\\n116\\t        RegIndex vd = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 4, 0);\\n117\\t        RegIndex vn = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 9, 5);\\n118\\t        RegIndex vm = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 20, 16);\\n119\\t\\n120\\t        // opcode LSB distinguishes FMLA (0x19, bit0=1) from FMLS (0x1B, bit0=1):\\n121\\t        // FMLA: opcode & 1 = 1, FMLS: opcode & 1 = 1... wait:\\n122\\t        // 0x19 = 11001 -> bit0=1; 0x1B = 11011 -> bit0=1. Both have bit0=1!\\n123\\t        // So we check the raw opcode: 0x19=FMLA, 0x1B=FMLS.\\n124\\t        // For FMLS only 16-bit elements are valid; 32/64-bit return Unknown.\\n125\\t        switch (size) {\\n126\\t          case 0: // 16-bit elements (half-precision)\\n127\\t            if (opcode == 0x19) {\\n128\\t                if (q)\\n129\\t                    return new FmlaQX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n130\\t                else\\n131\\t                    return new FmlaDX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n132\\t            } else { // 0x1B = FMLS\\n133\\t                if (q)\\n134\\t                    return new FmlsQX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n135\\t                else\\n136\\t                    return new FmlsDX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n137\\t            }\\n138\\t          case 1: // 32-bit elements (single-precision)\\n139\\t            // FMLS is not defined for single-precision scalar; FMLA is.\\n140\\t            if (opcode == 0x19) {\\n141\\t                if (q)\\n142\\t                    return new FmlaQX<uint32_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n143\\t                else\\n144\\t                    return new FmlaDX<uint32_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n145\\t            }\\n146\\t            return new Unknown64(machInst);\\n147\\t          default:\\n148\\t            return new Unknown64(machInst);\\n149\\t        }\\n150\\t    }\\n151\\t\\n152\\t    StaticInstPtr\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"uuid\":\"7d364036-9ef7-4caf-9ea4-372e7d1535e4\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:01:37.332Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"efd6e9d9-4866-4661-91d5-f2cdc33726e1\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"7d364036-9ef7-4caf-9ea4-372e7d1535e4\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d0f111ccd0a4b58f3a2abb4ff386c\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Now I need to fix the opcode extraction. `bits(machInst, 14, 10)` gives only 5 bits (bits 14,13,12,11,10). I need 6 bits (bits 15,14,13,12,11,10). Use `bits(machInst, 15, 10)`.\\n\\nAlso, the opcode comparison should be:- FMLS: `bits(15,10) = 0x04`- FMLA: `bits(15,10) = 0x0B`\\nBut actually, looking at the NEON decodeNeon3Same function, it uses `opcode = bits(machInst, 15, 13)` (3 bits) + the u bit from bit29. \\n\\nSo the actual NEON opcode is just 4 bits total, not 6. Let me reconsider how gem5 defines the opcode field for these scalar instructions. Looking at the NEON scalar three-same decoder, it extracts the opcode as a combination of bits from different positions in the instruction encoding.\\n\\nFor FMLA specifically, the opcode bits are 0b001, which means bit13 is 0 and bits15:14 are 00. I need to figure out what the corresponding bits are in the scalar FP encoding to understand how the same instruction maps across both formats.\\n\\nThe scalar FP FMLA uses opcode = 0x0B, while FMLS uses opcode = 0x04. The key insight is that the LSB (bit0) of the opcode distinguishes between them: when it's 1 we get FMLA, when it's 0 we get FMLS. So for the scalar FP format, I can check `opcode & 1` to determine the instruction type.\\n\\nNow I'm updating the code to use the full 6-bit opcode field and implement the conditional logic based on that LSB check. The NEON decoder uses a similar approach but with just 3 bits for the opcode field, which should align with the scalar FP encoding's lower bits.\",\"signature\":\"9d7ade7c994bf9d002e5b501120d27e194ea75a575a817188c0dc629ab16b15d\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":975,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":105702},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"ecb330f1-a83f-45dd-9ddf-b519653f195b\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:01:51.640Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"ecb330f1-a83f-45dd-9ddf-b519653f195b\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d0f111ccd0a4b58f3a2abb4ff386c\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Need to fix: `bits(machInst, 14, 10)` only gets 5 bits. Should be `bits(machInst, 15, 10)` for the full 6-bit opcode.\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":975,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":105702},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"b256b693-1a7b-41cf-875d-02b1316fdd87\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:01:52.870Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"b256b693-1a7b-41cf-875d-02b1316fdd87\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d0f111ccd0a4b58f3a2abb4ff386c\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_function_d1ub7qrx6emr_1\",\"name\":\"Edit\",\"input\":{\"replace_all\":false,\"file_path\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5/src/arch/arm/isa/formats/neon64.isa\",\"old_string\":\"output decoder {{\\nnamespace Aarch64\\n{\\n    // FMLA/FMLS: 31:24=00011110, 23:22=00, 21=1, 15=1, opcode in bits14:10\\n    // Encoding matches AdvSIMD scalar three-same; dispatch through\\n    // decodeNeonUThreeFpReg using the same (opcode, size, q) tuple.\\n    StaticInstPtr\\n    decodeFpMulMadd(ExtMachInst machInst)\\n    {\\n        uint8_t q      = bits(machInst, 30);\\n        uint8_t size   = bits(machInst, 23, 22);\\n        uint8_t opcode = bits(machInst, 14, 10);\\n\\n        RegIndex vd = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 4, 0);\\n        RegIndex vn = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 9, 5);\\n        RegIndex vm = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 20, 16);\\n\\n        // opcode LSB distinguishes FMLA (0x19, bit0=1) from FMLS (0x1B, bit0=1):\\n        // FMLA: opcode & 1 = 1, FMLS: opcode & 1 = 1... wait:\\n        // 0x19 = 11001 -> bit0=1; 0x1B = 11011 -> bit0=1. Both have bit0=1!\\n        // So we check the raw opcode: 0x19=FMLA, 0x1B=FMLS.\\n        // For FMLS only 16-bit elements are valid; 32/64-bit return Unknown.\\n        switch (size) {\\n          case 0: // 16-bit elements (half-precision)\\n            if (opcode == 0x19) {\\n                if (q)\\n                    return new FmlaQX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n                else\\n                    return new FmlaDX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n            } else { // 0x1B = FMLS\\n                if (q)\\n                    return new FmlsQX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n                else\\n                    return new FmlsDX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n            }\\n          case 1: // 32-bit elements (single-precision)\\n            // FMLS is not defined for single-precision scalar; FMLA is.\\n            if (opcode == 0x19) {\\n                if (q)\\n                    return new FmlaQX<uint32_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n                else\\n                    return new FmlaDX<uint32_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n            }\\n            return new Unknown64(machInst);\\n          default:\\n            return new Unknown64(machInst);\\n        }\\n    }\",\"new_string\":\"output decoder {{\\nnamespace Aarch64\\n{\\n    // FMLA/FMLS: 31:24=00011110, 23:22=00, 21=1, 15=1, opcode in bits15:10\\n    // These are reserved in scalar FP space but are valid AdvSIMD scalar\\n    // three-same instructions.  Dispatch based on the full 6-bit opcode.\\n    StaticInstPtr\\n    decodeFpMulMadd(ExtMachInst machInst)\\n    {\\n        uint8_t q      = bits(machInst, 30);\\n        uint8_t size   = bits(machInst, 23, 22);\\n        // Full 6-bit opcode: bits(15,10).  FMLS=0x04, FMLA=0x0B.\\n        uint8_t opcode = bits(machInst, 15, 10);\\n\\n        RegIndex vd = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 4, 0);\\n        RegIndex vn = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 9, 5);\\n        RegIndex vm = (RegIndex)(uint8_t)bits(machInst, 20, 16);\\n\\n        // opcode & 1: 0=FMLS, 1=FMLA\\n        // For FMLS only 16-bit elements are valid; 32/64-bit return Unknown.\\n        switch (size) {\\n          case 0: // 16-bit elements (half-precision)\\n            if (opcode & 1) { // FMLA\\n                if (q)\\n                    return new FmlaQX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n                else\\n                    return new FmlaDX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n            } else { // FMLS\\n                if (q)\\n                    return new FmlsQX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n                else\\n                    return new FmlsDX<uint16_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n            }\\n          case 1: // 32-bit elements (single-precision)\\n            // FMLS is not defined for single-precision scalar; only FMLA.\\n            if (opcode & 1) { // FMLA\\n                if (q)\\n                    return new FmlaQX<uint32_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n                else\\n                    return new FmlaDX<uint32_t>(machInst, vd, vn, vm);\\n            }\\n            return new Unknown64(machInst);\\n          default:\\n            return new Unknown64(machInst);\\n        }\\n    }\"}}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":975,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":105702,\"output_tokens\":1725,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"8bba8c60-04cb-453f-a169-6f0928067631\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:02:14.845Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"8bba8c60-04cb-453f-a169-6f0928067631\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"520da623-e17e-4efe-b292-47222de157e3\",\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\