role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_function_otsrvm7q9vqp_1\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"3694\\t    // FMLA/FMLS: 31:24=00011110, 23:22=00, 21=1, 15=1\\n3695\\t    // These are reserved in scalar FP space; they are actually AdvSIMD\\n3696\\t    // scalar three-same.  Catch them before isFpDataProc2Source.\\n3697\\t    inline constexpr auto isFpMulMadd = bitPatternMatcher<\\n3698\\t        MachInst,\\n3699\\t        31, 10,\\n3700\\t        '0','0','0','1', // op0: bits31:28=0001\\n3701\\t        '1','1','1',\\n3702\\t        '0','0',         // op1: bits27:24=0110 (bit24=0 already enforced)\\n3703\\t        '0','X','X','X', // op2: bit23=0, bits22:20=XXX\\n3704\\t        'X','X','X','1', // op3: bits19:16=XXXX, bit15=1\\n3705\\t        '1','X','X','X','X'>(); // op3: bits14:10=1XXXX\\n3706\\t\\n3707\\t    inline constexpr auto isFpDataProc1Source = bitPatternMatcher<\\n3708\\t        MachInst,\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"uuid\":\"236e0c95-d057-4420-b8d2-f3b894812284\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:12:31.631Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"41b110d3-cc4b-4d85-b1da-076cb40b1c1e\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"236e0c95-d057-4420-b8d2-f3b894812284\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d119f9d27b38a0807ae41d81ab172\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Now I need to fix the pattern to use 'X' for bit15 instead of '1'. The pattern should be:\\n```\\n'0','0','0','1', // op0: bits31:28=0001\\n'1','1','1',\\n'0','0',         // op1: bits27:24=0110 (bit24=0 already enforced)\\n'0','X','X','X', // op2: bit23=0, bits22:20=XXX\\n'X','X','X','X', // op3: bits19:16=XXXX, bit15=X\\n'X','X','X','X','X'>(); // op3: bits14:10=XXXXX\\n\\n\\n```\\n\\nThat gives me 22 characters total. Let me double-check the bit layout: bits 31-10 should map to the operator bits, and I need to verify the character count matches up correctly.\\n\\nSo I'm mapping out the bit ranges: bits 31-28 get four operator bits, bits 27-25 get three, bits 24-23 get two, bits 22-20 get three, and bits 19-16 get four, which totals 16 bits so far.\\n\\nNow I'm finishing the mapping with bits 15-10, which gives me another 6 bits for a total of 22 bits across all the operator sections.\\n\\n```\\n'0','0','0','1', // op0: bits31:28=0001\\n'1','1','1',       // op1: bits27:25=111\\n'0','0',           // op2: bits24:23=00\\n'0','X','X','X',   // op3: bits22:20=0XX\\n'X','X','X','X',   // op4: bits19:16=XXXX\\n'X','X','X','X','X'>(); // op5: bits15:10=XXXXX\\n```\\n\\nNow I need to update the decoder function to use the 5-bit opcode field instead of the 6-bit one.\",\"signature\":\"f37149fe1481a8663305135b3be418b3c3f56fbe8d42c436b582ffb2147588aa\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":147,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":122761},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"401182bd-f8dd-4937-9e12-8e4da224016c\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:12:45.260Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"401182bd-f8dd-4937-9e12-8e4da224016c\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":