\"thinking\":\"Now I understand the full picture. Looking at `decodeFpConvFixed` (line 2629):1. It checks `s = bits(machInst, 29)`. If `s=1`, returns Unknown.\\n2. For `0x1e2e1000`: bit29=0, so this passes.\\n3. It then uses `switchVal = bits(machInst, 20, 16)` = `bits(20,16)` of `0x1e2e1000` = `(0x1e2e1000 >> 16) & 0x1F` = `0x0E` = 14.\\n\\n\\n4. The switch statement only handles cases 0x00-0x05, 0x08, 0x09, and 0x0e, so when `switchVal = 14` lands in the default case, it returns Unknown. I see the issue now—`isConvFloatPFixedP` matches because the bit constraints aren't strict enough to exclude this instruction.\\n\\nMy change tightens the pattern by requiring `bit22=1`, which correctly excludes FMLA/FMLS (which have `bit22=0`), but I'm second-guessing whether this breaks FCVT instructions. Let me trace through the FCVT encoding: `0x1e220010` has `bit22=1`, `bit21=0`, and `bit20=0`, which means `switchVal = bits(20,16) = 0x00`. This falls into case 0x00 of the switch and calls `fcvtns`, so my pattern change should still work correctly.\\n\\nNow I need to rebuild and test, but first I'm realizing there's a critical issue with the pattern group boundaries. In the `bitPatternMatcher`, groups are created based on the 2-bit groups in the 22-bit range, and my `'1','X','X','X'` pattern spans across groups in a way that might not be what I intended. I'm checking whether setting `bit22=1` breaks valid FCVT instructions—for `fcvtzu` with opcode 0x0B, `switchVal = bits(20,16) = 0x0B` falls into case 11, which returns `FailUnimplemented`, so it won't actually decode anything but that's acceptable. I'm realizing my fix might actually work for this case too. Let me just rebuild and test it.\\n\\nActually, wait—I need to double-check how the groups are being consumed by the pattern matcher. With 22 bits total, that's 11 groups of 2 bits each, and I should verify my pattern is using exactly that many groups without going out of bounds. I've verified all 22 bits of the mask are accounted for across the pattern fields, and the logic checks out that bit22 must equal 1 to pass the constraint. Now I need to build and test this approach.\",\"signature\":\"711814a23aa3ef1999fd09bc5b43c6fafa9ca4e75dbb107ad88e1fcf56cfd96d\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":3229,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":133346},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"58014096-e830-47db-8e8c-076a1531c44e\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:18:41.731Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"58014096-e830-47db-8e8c-076a1531c44e\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d12fb3418a2b4f8dfca91f4c52e80\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"`decodeFpConvFixed` returns `Unknown` for `switchVal=14` (case 0x0E → `fcvtzs`, not the switchVal that FMLS gives). With my fix tightening `isConvFloatPFixedP` to `bit22=1`, FMLS with `bit22=0` will no longer match. Let me rebuild and test.\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":3229,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":133346},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"9ed8a6d3-cf67-4823-80b9-d827886df0af\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:18:43.659Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"9ed8a6d3-cf67-4823-80b9-d827886df0af\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agent