m);\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"uuid\":\"64c79930-ef1f-43ab-905f-504ce68b2b3b\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:21:29.073Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"b98bfa73-09e6-48da-abbe-87d98fdd957c\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"64c79930-ef1f-43ab-905f-504ce68b2b3b\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d13b9c1b281f0634fdb5dd3587879\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"I need to add the guard for FMLA/FMLS (bit21=1) in decodeFpDataProc2Source. The guard should check if bit21=1 and return Unknown64. FMLA and FMLS have:- bit21=1- bit20=0 (always)\\n- bit15=0 (always)- So bit20=0 AND bit15=0 distinguishes from FMSUB/FNMADD/FNMSUB.So:```cppif (bits(machInst, 21) && !bits(machInst, 20) && !bits(machInst, 15))\\n    return new Unknown64(machInst);```Wait but actually, after tightening isFpDataProc1Source with bit22=1, and tightening isConvFloatPFixedP with bit22=1, the FMLA/FMLS with bit22=0 should no longer match those patterns. But they could still potentially match isFpDataProc2Source if the pattern also has bit22=X. Let me check.isFpDataProc2Source pattern:```'X','0','X','1', // op0'1','1','1','0','X', // op1: bits27:26=0X -> bit26=X, bit27=1\\n```I see - this pattern allows bit26 to be flexible while keeping bit27 fixed at 1, so the guard needs to check that specific combination of bit21=1, bit20=0, and bit15=0 to properly distinguish FMLA/FMLS from other instructions.\",\"signature\":\"c25e1e2c2b5561d2a2a0526ef47bb262e6ca082804714d5771cf918a0c4d0015\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":512,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":140591},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"305210bf-2189-4dbb-9647-1afebd3fc50a\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:21:40.564Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"305210bf-2189-4dbb-9647-1afebd3fc50a\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d13b9c1b281f0634fdb5dd3587879\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_function_d6b7mgsgk8k1_1\",\"name\":\"Edit\",\"input\":{\"replace_all\":false,\"file_path\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5/src/arch/arm/isa/formats/aarch64.isa\",\"old_string\":\"    StaticInstPtr\\n    decodeFpDataProc2Source(ExtMachInst machInst)\\n    {\\n        if (bits(machInst, 31) ||\\n                bits(machInst, 29)) {\\n            return new Unknown64(machInst);\\n        }\\n        RegIndex rd = (RegIndex)(uint32_t)bits(machInst,  4,  0);\\n        RegIndex rn = (RegIndex)(uint32_t)bits(machInst,  9,  5);\\n        RegIndex rm = (RegIndex)(uint32_t)bits(machInst, 20, 16);\\n        uint8_t switchVal = (bits(machInst, 15, 12) << 0) |\\n                            (bits(machInst, 23, 22) << 4);\",\"new_string\":\"    StaticInstPtr\\n    decodeFpDataProc2Source(ExtMachInst machInst)\\n    {\\n        if (bits(machInst, 31) ||\\n                bits(machInst, 29)) {\\n            return new Unknown64(machInst);\\n        }\\n\\n        // FMLA/FMLS (bit21=1, bit20=0, bit15=0) are rese