ystem uses AtomicSimpleCPU with bare-metal workload. gem5 maps the ELF to a default physical address. The entry point might not be 0x10000. But regardless of the actual PC, the instruction encoding 0x1e2e1000 is what gem5 is trying to decode. Let me reconsider whether this instruction is actually at the entry point or if it's coming from a different location in the ELF. Looking at the ELF hexdump more carefully, the instruction at 0x10000 is indeed `0x1e2e1000` and the entry point is also 0x10000, so this IS the first instruction being executed. Now I need to trace through gem5's decode logic to see if there's a mismatch between what the pattern matcher expects and what the instruction actually contains.\\n\\nLet me check the SVE integer decode path to see if that's where the issue lies.\",\"signature\":\"631acedb71589e143c69174e546fdf34c2d6fba1cf8f5084cc650b881425b303\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":489,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":161307},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"c0a9e398-4a0e-467e-bbbf-fce560fca3aa\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T03:55:25.292Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"c0a9e398-4a0e-467e-bbbf-fce560fca3aa\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d1b97fa42198cf2570ffe170bfbfe\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me check the full routing path including SVE decoders.\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":489,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":161307},\"service_tier