- bit29=0 ✓\\n- bit28=1 ✓\\n- bit27=1 ✓\\n- bit26=1 ✓\\n- bit25=1 ✓\\n- bit24=0 ✓\\n\\n0x2e = 00101110 = bit23:16\\n- bit23=0 ✓\\n- bit22=0 ✓\\n- bit21=1 ✓\\n- bit20=0 ✓\\n\\nSo bit26=1 and bit25=1, which should work with the pattern since both are wildcards. But my earlier Python simulation disagreed—let me recalculate the mask correctly this time. I'm tracing through the recursion to verify the mask calculation: starting with msb=31, lsb=10, and 22 characters, it correctly computes mask=0xf9c00000 by recursing down through each position and accumulating the bit shifts. Now I'm checking the match computation the same way, starting from position 31.\\n\\nComputing the match bits...\",\"signature\":\"5c757110a930828472d692d2c41ed2dcd6b21db43beb9a52b499c775bd63b874\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":377,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":96512},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"136bf696-ab35-4662-bc51-c3c2e1381b5b\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:22:55.445Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"136bf696-ab35-4662-bc51-c3c2e1381b5b\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d220f822c9867207e9e5d2ed75d1b\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The generated code has `'0','0'` correctly. Let me add debug to trace the actual execution:\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":377,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":96512},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"66dd0922-651e-486c-85f7-64