,\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"OK so `main.isa` includes `formats/formats.isa` which in turn includes `formats/aarch64.isa`. And the ISA compiler generates the .cc and .hh files from these.\\n\\nThe decoder files are included in the generated decoder.cc:\\n```cpp\\n#include \\\"base/compiler.hh\\\"\\n#include \\\"decoder-g.cc.inc\\\"\\n#include \\\"decoder.hh\\\"\\n#include \\\"decode-method.cc.inc\\\"\\n```\\n\\nWait, looking at the generated decoder.cc:\\n```cpp\\n#include \\\"base/compiler.hh\\\"\\n#include \\\"decoder-g.cc.inc\\\"\\n#include \\\"decoder.hh\\\"\\n#include \\\"decode-method.cc.inc\\\"\\n\\n\\n```\\n\\n`decoder-ns.cc.inc` is NOT included in `decoder.cc`. So where is `decodeFpAdvSIMD` from `decoder-ns.cc.inc` being used? Looking at `decode-method.cc.inc`, line 2914 shows the decoder is calling `decodeFpAdvSIMD<GenericDecoder>`, which must be defined somewhere in the non-static decoder path.\\n\\n`decode-method.cc.inc` is included in `decoder.cc`, so I need to check if `decoder-ns.cc.inc` is also included or if `decodeFpAdvSIMD` is coming from a template instantiation elsewhere. Let me search through the generated files to see which one actually defines `decodeFpAdvSIMD`.\\n\\n```\",\"signature\":\"993af84b65fa35ed74e0bb1250ab6e14764fa660b9cf9774cec551bb11f1914b\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":255,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":100146},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"79ac2c8f-f335-4243-9815-ae80d637c9a6\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:26:48.842Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"79ac2c8f-f335-4243-9815-ae80d637c9a6\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a