78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d25cf4b8ead172b7e8c029be14644\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"The `ExtMachInst` ends at line 203. After that, there's `BitUnion32(Affinity)`. So the last bitfield in `ExtMachInst` is `Bitfield<4>` at line 199 (bit 4). Then there's `Bitfield<11,8>` (ltcoproc), and the `EndBitUnion` at line 203.\\n\\nWait, but `Bitfield<11,8>` extends beyond bit 4. Is this correct? Let me think again...\\n\\nLooking at the ARM bitfield extraction syntax:- `Bitfield<11,8>` = bits 11 through 8, which is 4 bits\\n\\n\\n- `Bitfield<7,6>` = bits 7 through 6, which is 2 bits\\n- `Bitfield<7,4>` = bits 7 through 4, which is 4 bits\\n- `Bitfield<4>` = just bit 4\\n\\nThese bitfield definitions are all sub-fields within the 32-bit `instBits` space. But if the BitUnion ends at bit 4, how can there be bitfield<11,8>? Unless the BitUnion includes bits up through 31 (the entire `instBits` range), and these various bitfield definitions are all valid subfields within that space.\\n\\nThe `uint32_t instBits` stores the raw instruction, so any bitfield extraction like `Bitfield<11,8>` would read from that same 32-bit storage. But the BitUnion definition itself must span the full range—probably bits 31:0—to encompass all these overlapping bitfield definitions.\\n\\nNow I'm wondering if there's a bitfield defined for the instruction opcode that overlaps with my pattern check at bits 31:28. I need to look more carefully at the type definitions to see what's actually being extracted. I'm seeing the rest of the bitfield definitions for the instruction encoding, and there's a critical mismatch: `encoding` spans bits 27-25, but I'm checking bit 28, which falls outside this range. In my pattern, character 3 should map to bit 28, yet the `encoding` field definition doesn't include that bit. I need to check whether there's another bitfield covering bit 28 or if there's a structural conflict in how these fields are defined.\",\"signature\":\"5a83221d1bc4004108adc4919f1bf22ab4ab5662584ce8ae4aae80e437942f1c\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":126574},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"c075dc11-9d7f-43e4-b250-1aead3fad667\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:38:54.371Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"c075dc11-9d7f-43e4-b250-1aead3fad667\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d25cf4b8ead172b7e8c029be14644\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me look for what covers bits 31-28 in ExtMachInst:\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":126574},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"7e23ce8e-2d9d-444c-bb48-393ea7c9b090\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:38:54.893Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"7e23ce8e-2d9d-444c-bb48-393ea7c9b090\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d25cf4b8ead172b7e8c029be14644\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_function_ztulxa08oe55_1\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5/src/arch/arm/types.hh\",\"offset\":56,\"limit\":30}}],\"