n see it reads the condition status and control registers, then initializes the floating-point operation operands by reading from the register file and extracting the data into temporary variables. Looking at the template instantiation markers, I see this is the scalar variant where each operand occupies a single register—the union confirms this with 4 bytes per operand. The key distinction is that this uses VecElemContainer instead of VecRegContainer, which makes sense for scalar floating-point operations.\\n\\nBut wait, these declarations at lines 247972 and 247976 don't actually have matching definitions in the file. The template definitions that should instantiate them aren't present in exec-ns.cc.inc. This suggests the scalar versions might be defined elsewhere, possibly in exec-g.cc.inc. Let me search for where these template instantiations are actually implemented.\",\"signature\":\"509fa5adf4ae1ef72cf444a45d74b5766ad2edf6ce29e7116edf6101064fb009\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":3,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":71469},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"8822e9b7-5877-4579-8e20-3c9b909961f9\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:07:46.949Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"8822e9b7-5877-4579-8e20-3c9b909961f9\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d1e6876f7a089f56ad3ed6cb40928\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Let me search ALL generated files for the actual definition:\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":287,\"output_tokens