the pattern expects 1, so this one fails too. I'm continuing to verify `isAdvSIMD3Same` and the rest of the patterns in this chain.\\n\\nAfter working through all of them, `isFpMulMadd` is the first pattern that actually matches, which means it correctly routes to `decodeFpMulMadd`. When I decode `0x1e2e1000`, it extracts the register indices and operation type correctly, which should work properly.\\n\\nNow I'm wondering if the issue is actually with how `FmlsDX` is defined or if it's just returning an `Unknown64` object after all. Let me look more closely at the `decodeFpMulMadd` function to see what's happening there.\\n\\nExamining the decode logic...\\n\\nI'm checking the switch case for `size=0` (16-bit half-precision) and routing to the appropriate FMLS or FMLA variant based on the opcode bit. For `0x1e2e1000`, this should map to the scalar 16-bit FMLS instruction with `q=0`, which should instantiate `FmlsDX<uint16_t>`. The question is whether this instruction class actually exists and has a proper execute method defined. The `FmlsDX<uint16_t>` constructor is being called, but the execute method for this type might not be instantiated or defined in the compiled binary, even though the template definition exists elsewhere in the compilation unit. Let me check if this specific instantiation is actually available.\",\"signature\":\"aa04858afdea28ff7aaff302c59174cc06a1a7c2ba2fa8d239af6c457b496a2d\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":111798},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"f588df3a-97a3-4430-b325-41e8c50d6415\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T04:32:34.948Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping