nstructor—meaning the `Unknown64` execute code isn't being invoked when the panic occurs, which suggests the execution path is different from what I initially thought. I'm realizing the distinction between `decodeInst` (which constructs the instruction) and `execute` (which runs it). The debug print I'm looking at is only in the execute method, so even though `decodeInst` successfully creates an `Unknown64` object, I wouldn't see that output unless the execute actually gets called—which means the panic is happening somewhere else in the execution path.\\n\\nLet me step back and think about this differently. The `atomic_simple_cpu` is calling `advancePC` with a fault, which suggests the fault handling is what's triggering the panic, not necessarily the decode itself. The debug output shows `advancePCERKNSt3__110shared_ptrI` indicating a `RefCountingPtr<FaultBase>` is being passed, which means there's a fault object involved in the execution flow.\\n\\nNow I need to figure out what `UndefinedInstruction::invoke` is actually doing when it gets called with the unknown instruction.\",\"signature\":\"aa8742c4dc4730b7a861eee6e12c1953e9050501091d9d55cee45fd094c57eb5\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":218,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":79,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":143774},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"213a60a7-7f50-46eb-8586-0ee0983c84d3\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:12:28.025Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"213a60a7-7f50-46eb-8586-0ee0983c84d3\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d2dafd9e387611ae4a8eed9ab6b5a\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"ty