\"uuid\":\"6441c089-fc41-4b89-9ce1-e47b13ee3a6a\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:45:45.228Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"6441c089-fc41-4b89-9ce1-e47b13ee3a6a\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"520da623-e17e-4efe-b292-47222de157e3\",\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_function_hgtx9b1vmra5_1\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"285\\t        interpImage = objFile->getInterpreter()->buildImage();\\n286\\t}\\n287\\t\\n288\\tvoid\\n289\\tProcess::initState()\\n290\\t{\\n291\\t    if (contextIds.empty())\\n292\\t        fatal(\\\"Process %s is not associated with any HW contexts!\\\\n\\\", name());\\n293\\t\\n294\\t    // first thread context for this process... initialize & enable\\n295\\t    ThreadContext *tc = system->threads[contextIds[0]];\\n296\\t\\n297\\t    // mark this context as active so it will start ticking.\\n298\\t    tc->activate();\\n299\\t\\n300\\t    pTable->initState();\\n301\\t\\n302\\t    initVirtMem.reset(new SETranslatingPortProxy(\\n303\\t                tc, SETranslatingPortProxy::Always));\\n304\\t\\n305\\t    // load object file into target memory\\n306\\t    image.write(*initVirtMem);\\n307\\t    interpImage.write(*initVirtMem);\\n308\\t}\\n309\\t\\n310\\tDrainState\\n311\\tProcess::drain()\\n312\\t{\\n313\\t    fds->updateFileOffsets();\\n314\\t    return DrainState::Drained;\\n315\\t}\\n316\\t\\n317\\tvoid\\n318\\tProcess::allocateMem(Addr vaddr, int64_t size, bool clobber)\\n319\\t{\\n320\\t    const auto page_size = pTable->pageSize();\\n321\\t\\n322\\t    const Addr page_addr = roundDown(vaddr, page_size);\\n323\\t\\n324\\t    // Check if the page has been mapped by other cores if not to clobber.\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"uuid\":\"f9ad7e97-d4fb-48a5-b03a-e5952f6a581f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:45:45.358Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"6441c089-fc41-4b89-9ce1-e47b13ee3a6a\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"f9ad7e97-d4fb-48a5-b03a-e5952f6a581f\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d35898780de59edb9ebbee9d200fa\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"`Process::initState()` doesn't set the PC. Let me find the `BareMetalWorkload::initState` which was mentioned in the config comment: \\\"BareMetalWorkload::initState() (C++) sets PC to ELF entry and SP to 0x80010000\\\".\",\"signature\":\"a4b1cab9f364840b3d7aec605e308675f44340f7ffa2129573ac9ef2e6e4a47d\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":218,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":579,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":72996},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"09a03d08-187d-49b4-bcdf-7b48fc428c52\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:45:49.074Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"09a03d08-187d-49b4-bcdf-7b48fc428c52\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d