\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d361f1989d75204972ff4d4f3d846\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The fix: after `pc.pc(entry)`, set `pc.aarch64(true)` for ARM64 binaries. I need to check if the process is `ArmBareMetalProcess64`.\\n\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":218,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":395,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":81508},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"50014361-7035-42e0-8af0-cc9abdcbb591\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:48:22.189Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"50014361-7035-42e0-8af0-cc9abdcbb591\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d361f1989d75204972ff4d4f3d846\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_function_oedtgav7m83w_1\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/gem5/src/arch/arm/bare_metal/process.hh\",\"offset\":58,\"limit\":20}}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":\"tool_use\",\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":218,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":395,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":81508,\"output_tokens\":296,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"21687a45-87f0-402d-a132-76148e9e1d93\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:48:23.240Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"21687a45-87f0-402d-a132-76148e9e1d93\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"promptId\":\"f0504b47-17c9-4bb4-afb0-5fee28a51291\",\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"call_function_oedtgav7m83w_1\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"58\\t};\\n59\\t\\n60\\tclass ArmBareMetalProcess64 : public ArmProcess64\\n61\\t{\\n62\\t  public:\\n63\\t    ArmBareMetalProcess64(const ProcessParams &params,\\n64\\t                          loader::ObjectFile *objFile, loader::Arch _arch);\\n65\\t\\n66\\t  protected:\\n67\\t    void initState() override;\\n68\\t\\n69\\t    uint32_t armHwcapImpl() const override;\\n70\\t    uint64_t armHwcapImpl2() const override;\\n71\\t};\\n72\\t\\n73\\t} // namespace ArmISA\\n74\\t\\n75\\t} // namespace gem5\\n76\\t\\n77\\t#endif // __ARCH_ARM_BARE_METAL_PROCESS_HH__\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"uuid\":\"d79041b7-e4b2-4347-8012-2d797ef38d53\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:48:23.368Z\",\"sourceToolAssistantUUID\":\"21687a45-87f0-402d-a132-76148e9e1d93\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"d79041b7-e4b2-4347-8012-2d797ef38d53\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d362749ae0bed0287c9d6f924c032\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"I can add a method to ArmBareMetalProcess64 that returns the arch, then use dynamic_cast in BareMetalWorkload::initState(). Or simpler: add a method `bool is64Bit()` that returns true for ArmBareMetalProcess64.\\n\\nActually, the simplest fix: after `proc->initState()` sets up the CPSR (which includes mode information), the CPSR in AArch64 state would have specific characteristics. But the cleanest fix is to add a helper method.\\n\\nActually, let me think about this differently. The BareMetalWorkload::initState() is a template - it's used for all bare-metal configurations. \\n\\nFor AArch64, I need to set the AArch64 bit in the PC state. I can use dynamic_cast to check if the process is ArmBareMetalProcess64, then set pc.aarch64(true) if it is. Let me verify this approach will work by checking the includes in workload.cc.\",\"signature\":\"b30435b83dc03548c0c97ba022be2b1b22902df9a828ea303eebb5b2c7133ec4\"}],\"model\":\"MiniMax-M2.7\",\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":218,\"output_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":176,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":82123},\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"type\":\"assistant\",\"uuid\":\"774809e5-0877-41e8-a318-787958e36932\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-04-02T05:48:31.816Z\",\"userType\":\"external\",\"entrypoint\":\"cli\",\"cwd\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build\",\"sessionId\":\"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1\",\"version\":\"2.1.87\",\"gitBranch\":\"stable\",\"slug\":\"proud-popping-falcon\"}\n{\"parentUuid\":\"774809e5-0877-41e8-a318-787958e36932\",\"isSidechain\":true,\"agentId\":\"a5d384807705efc78\",\"message\":{\"id\":\"061d362749ae0bed0287c9d6f924c032\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_function_g95lrzqc073m_1\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-f