{"parentUuid":"22b175b0-bdee-4af6-b431-8caef991df0f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"061d376915277dfc228a4a4c34f7fc8a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The ELF looks correct - it's a simple test with MOV and RET instructions. The panic is happening at 0x00000000 which is strange - that means the PC is being set to 0 after the RET instruction. This is probably because there's no proper exit handling in the bare-metal binary.\n\nActually wait - the panic is because it tries to execute an instruction at 0x00000000 after the RET - this is expected behavior for a bare-metal program that doesn't have proper exit handling.\n\nLet me check if gem5 is actually loading the ELF properly and executing the instructions. The debug shows \"DEBUG Unknown64::execute machInst=0x400000000\" - that address 0x400000000 looks wrong. The instruction should be at 0x400000 (physical) but it's showing as 0x400000000.\n\nWait - this could be a PC state issue. The PC is being set to address 0x400000000 instead of 0x400000. That's 4GB higher! This is likely the virtual address being used directly without translation.\n\nActually looking more carefully at the debug output - it says \"machInst=0x400000000\" which is weird. The instruction at address 0x400000 is \"d2800000\" (mov x0, #0x0). But the machInst is showing as 0x400000000... This might be the full ExtMachInst with the high bits set to something.\n\nLet me check if the test is actually running more instructions before the panic. The simpler approach is that the test ELF is too simple and has no proper exit - it returns and tries to execute at address 0 which causes the panic.\n\nThis is actually progress! The decoder is now working for AARCH64 mode. The issue is that the bare-metal binary doesn't have proper exit handling.\n\nLet me check if there's a way to make the test exit properly, or if we should use a different test approach.\n","signature":"5976f4b2a7d12175f1555cd9a7058fca3eee59b12b566c5b116397cc58ccb13c"}],"model":"MiniMax-M2.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":140675,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"service_tier":"standard"},"type":"assistant","uuid":"8ea58ef7-5cd7-4203-bb1a-e49213659fdb","timestamp":"2026-04-02T05:54:11.484Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build","sessionId":"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1","version":"2.1.87","gitBranch":"stable","slug":"proud-popping-falcon"}
