{"parentUuid":"5289cc02-df5c-41e2-bd65-110254666959","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"061d37847d07cd179ee3f5ee13fc77fc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The issue is clear now. The ELF doesn't have any exit syscall - it just has a RET instruction at the end. In bare-metal mode, after the RET, the PC goes to some invalid address (0x0 or 0x400000000), which causes an \"unknown instruction\" error.\n\nIn real bare-metal, the behavior after RET would be undefined or it would hang. But in gem5, when PC goes to an invalid address, it tries to decode an instruction there and fails.\n\nThe solution is to either:\n1. Add an infinite loop (like `b .` or `wfi` at the end of the program) to prevent PC from falling through\n2. Use a proper exit mechanism that gem5 understands\n\nLet me check if there's a way to make the simulation exit cleanly. In gem5, there are special \"exit\" events that can be triggered. One common approach is to use the `m5 exit` instruction or a syscall.\n\nActually, the simpler fix is to just add an infinite loop at the end of the test program. Let me create a simple test ELF that has an infinite loop at the end, so the simulation can run without crashing.\n\nBut wait - the user said \"先处理其他任务\" (handle other tasks first). Let me ask what they want to do next, or summarize the current status.\n\nActually, I should provide a summary to the user about the current state and what the issues are:\n\n1. QEMU is built and works\n2. gem5 decoder now correctly routes AARCH64 instructions\n3. But the test ELF files don't have proper exit handling, causing crashes after program finishes\n\nLet me summarize and ask for next steps.\n","signature":"874bcf5ffe69b685240ab3b578fce2ba232898c165e95955c3ee5f483bc7a9c7"}],"model":"MiniMax-M2.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":143915,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"service_tier":"standard"},"type":"assistant","uuid":"8df53835-e1b4-4ec5-8614-5634e9a9f495","timestamp":"2026-04-02T05:54:38.948Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build","sessionId":"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1","version":"2.1.87","gitBranch":"stable","slug":"proud-popping-falcon"}
{"parentUuid":"8df53835-e1b4-4ec5-8614-5634e9a9f495","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"061d37847d07cd179ee3f5ee13fc77fc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n**gem5 状态分析:**\n\n1. **Decoder 修复进展** ✅\n   - AARCH64=1 bit 现在正确设置\n   - FMADD/FMLA/FMLS 正确路由到 `decodeFpMulMadd`\n   - 指令被成功解码\n\n2. **运行时问题** ⚠️\n   - 测试 ELF 执行完毕后 RET 到 0x0 或 0x400000000\n   - 无效地址导致 \"unknown instruction\" panic\n   - ELF 缺少退出机制 (如 `wfi` 或 `b .` 无限循环)\n\n3. **下一步选项:**\n   - A: 在测试 ELF 末尾添加无限循环\n   - B: 使用 gem5 专用退出指令\n   - C: 先生成有效的测试用例\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\n**当前已就绪:**\n- QEMU 10.2.91 已构建 (`/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build/qemu-system-aarch64`)\n- gem5 decoder AARCH64 路由已修复\n\n**问题:** 测试 ELF 缺少退出处理。请指示:\n1. 继续修复 gem5 退出机制?\n2. 生成带有正确退出流的测试用例?\n3. 提交当前代码更改?"}],"model":"MiniMax-M2.5","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2647,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":156352,"output_tokens":615,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"service_tier":"standard"},"type":"assistant","uuid":"7f6c1172-adc7-41d3-95da-9f2d4b44574f","timestamp":"2026-04-02T05:54:39.129Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/wangxu/1-project/sdc-fuzzing/qemu/build","sessionId":"d910793e-44d5-4b76-a978-fb98052552f1","version":"2.1.87","gitBranch":"stable","slug":"proud-popping-falcon"}
